window.EAX_SEARCH = [{"t":"Further reading","u":"further-reading.html","s":"Where to go outside EA Explorer: the standards it follows, the open-source parts it is built on, the code and the videos.","w":"EA Explorer itself - The EA Explorer YouTube channel https://www.youtube.com/@ea-explorer-os : short videos by role. - The code on GitHub https://github.com/gauravvermaea/EA-Explorer : the source, the releases and how to report a problem or suggest a change. The standards it follows - The TOGAF Standard https://www.opengroup.org/togaf , from The Open Group: the Architecture Development Method ADM that EA Explorer's projects follow, and the content metamodel its models can use. - ArchiMate https://www.opengroup.org/archimate-forum/archimate-overview , from The Open Group: the modelling language EA Explorer's metamodel and drawn views use. - The Model Context Protocol https://modelcontextprotocol.io : how your own AI assistant talks to EA Explorer. - OData https://www.odata.org : the feed Power BI and Excel read EA Explorer's models through. - OpenAPI https://www.openapis.org : how EA Explorer's REST API is described its own pages are at /api/docs in every installation . The open-source parts it is built on - PostgreSQL https://www.postgresql.org : the database. - Keycloak https://www.keycloak.org : sign-in, single sign-on and multi-factor sign-in. - Apache Superset https://superset.apache.org : the reports and dashboards. - Mayan EDMS https://www.mayan-edms.com : document management in projects. - draw.io https://www.drawio.com : the drawn views. - Docker https://docs.docker.com : what every part runs in. - Jenkins https://www.jenkins.io : the operations pipelines. Every part and its licence is listed in EA Explorer itself, on System Admin › Settings › Licences."},{"t":"EA Explorer","u":"index.html","s":"A free, open-source enterprise architecture repository you run yourself: models, views, reports, projects and AI, in one place.","w":"EA Explorer keeps your organisation's architecture in one repository: the capabilities, value streams, processes, applications, data and technology, how they relate, and how they change over time. People draw views and run reports from it, architecture projects follow the TOGAF ADM with it, and your own AI assistant can read, analyse and change it with your permissions. It is free and open source AGPL-3.0 , with no charge per user, per object or per module, and it runs where you choose: a laptop, one server, or a machine in your cloud. Start with your role Each page says what EA Explorer has for you, how it is put together, and the tasks you will do, with a How do I page for each. You are Start here --- --- System Admin : you run the installation What EA Explorer has for System Admins roles/system-admin.md Model Admin : you look after models and their metamodels What EA Explorer has for Model Admins roles/model-admin.md Project Admin : you run architecture projects What EA Explorer has for Project Admins roles/project-admin.md A user : you find, change, draw and report on the architecture What EA Explorer has for users roles/user.md An industry model maker : you build reference models for an industry What EA Explorer has for industry model makers roles/industry-modeller.md A developer : you bring data in and take it out What EA Explorer has for developers roles/developer.md Find a task How do I how-do-i/index.html lists every task, one page each, step by step. Each page prints cleanly or saves as a PDF: press Print or save as PDF at the top of the page. Install it Install and run install/index.html has a guide for each set-up: a laptop, a server, any server over SSH, backups, restores, a DR site, moving machines, certificates and more. In EA Explorer the same guides are on System Admin › Tools › Setup, where you give your own values the server's name, where the files are and every command is filled in for you. What is in the box - The metamodel : ArchiMate 4 and the TOGAF 10 content metamodel built in, or your own; edited, versioned, reviewed and pushed down to the models that use it. - Models : entities and relationships entered in forms and grids, loaded from Excel or CSV, or delivered by other systems; private until committed; tagged, compared, copied, split and merged back. - Views and diagrams : networks, impact, capability maps and heat maps, matrices, value stream maps, roadmaps and 49 standard views, all drawn from the repository when you open them; your own drawn views in the built-in draw.io. - Reports : 30 standard reports and dashboards, your own in the report designer, KPI trends, data quality, and an OData feed for Power BI and Excel. - Projects : architecture projects from 14 templates on the TOGAF 10 library 13 phases, 116 steps, 171 deliverables and artifacts , with stakeholders, key questions, principles, sign-off and documents. - AI : connect your own AI assistant through MCP; it works as you, with your permissions, and every change it proposes waits for your yes. - Running it : one command eax for everything, backups and restores, updates, health and alerts, a DR site kept in step, and Jenkins pipelines for the operations. Videos Short videos for each role are on the EA Explorer YouTube channel https://www.youtube.com/@ea-explorer-os . See Videos videos.md ."},{"t":"Videos","u":"videos.html","s":"Short videos for each role, on the EA Explorer YouTube channel.","w":"The videos are on the EA Explorer YouTube channel https://www.youtube.com/@ea-explorer-os . Each is a minute or two and shows one task, made from the How do I pages on this site, so the page and the video say the same thing. They are grouped by role, the same way as this site: Role Where to start --- --- System Admin What EA Explorer has for System Admins roles/system-admin.md Model Admin What EA Explorer has for Model Admins roles/model-admin.md Project Admin What EA Explorer has for Project Admins roles/project-admin.md Users What EA Explorer has for users roles/user.md Industry model makers What EA Explorer has for industry model makers roles/industry-modeller.md Developers What EA Explorer has for developers roles/developer.md Note The videos play from YouTube, so they need the internet. Everything else on this site works without it."},{"t":"What EA Explorer has for System Admins","u":"roles/system-admin.html","s":"You run the installation: who may sign in and what they may do, security, backups, updates, health and the machine itself.","w":"Who this is for The people who run an EA Explorer installation. In EA Explorer these are the Super Admin everything, including settings and the delete-everything commands and the IT Admin running it: health, backups, updates, containers, logs , helped by the User Admin people and their roles and the Auditor sees everything a Super Admin sees, changes nothing . What you have Everything you need is under System Admin in the menu bar, and on the machine in one command, eax . Area Where What it gives you --- --- --- Wizards System Admin › Wizards The common jobs guided step by step, each asking before it changes anything Settings System Admin › Settings Application settings currency, time zone, date formats , system settings upload sizes, keep-for times, the parts in use, the site's purpose , the banner, branding, licences, and Settings import and export People System Admin › Users and roles Who has which role, on the installation, each model and each project; how Keycloak roles and directory groups become EA Explorer roles Security System Admin › Security Who may reach EA Explorer IP allow lists per place and multi-factor sign-in Running System Admin › Running Health, alerts, the job queue, containers, logs, hosts, mounts, databases, secrets, site pairings, database maintenance, footprint, sizing and more Backups System Admin › Backups and restores Backups now and on a schedule, restores, and disaster recovery Updates System Admin › Updates Moving to a newer release, with a backup first and a way back Tools System Admin › Tools The Command centre every eax command from the browser, with schedules , Setup the guides with your values filled in , the SQL window and the self-test Machine access System Admin › Machine access Tokens, API keys and client certificates for other systems On the machine, eax starts, stops, backs up, restores, updates, tests and repairs EA Explorer, on Windows, Linux and macOS .\\eax in PowerShell, ./eax.sh elsewhere . eax help lists every command. Jenkins, if you start it eax jenkins up , gives a pipeline for each command. How it is put together - Containers : EA Explorer runs as a set of Docker containers on one machine or several, when scaled out : the screens, the API and its jobs, the database PostgreSQL , sign-in Keycloak , reports Apache Superset , documents Mayan EDMS , the drawn views draw.io , the operations helper, backups, and a front door that every request passes through. System Admin › Running › Estate draws them. - People and roles : people sign in through Keycloak, from its own accounts or your directory. Their global roles Super Admin, IT Admin, User Admin, Auditor, Model Creator, Library Admin, Discovery Admin, Architecture Board, User come from Keycloak; their model roles Model Admin, Model Sub Admin, Committer, Architect, History Viewer, Report Viewer and project roles Project Admin, Lead Architect, Architect, Stakeholder and others are given on each model's and project's People tab. - Where the data lives : one PostgreSQL holds the repository and its parts in schemas of their own; documents, reports and the drawn views keep their own databases. Each can be moved to a server of its own System Admin › Running › Databases . - The config file : work/eaexplorer.env holds the settings the containers start with. Passwords and keys are separate files, one per container, never shown on screen System Admin › Running › Secrets shows each by name, its age and when it is due . - Backups : an infrastructure backup holds every database, the files, the config and the versions; an application backup holds one model. Both can be tagged, pinned, checked and restored whole or in part. Where to go next - The guides for installing and running it: Install and run ../install/index.html . - Every command: eax help on the machine, or ? › Command line eax in EA Explorer. - The API's own pages: /api/docs in your installation."},{"t":"What EA Explorer has for Model Admins","u":"roles/model-admin.html","s":"You look after models: who works in them, their metamodel, their quality, their versions, and how they are copied, split and merged.","w":"Who this is for People with the Model Admin role on a model given on that model's People tab , and the Model Sub Admin who helps them. A Model Creator a global role may make new models; a Library Admin looks after the model library. What you have Area Where What it gives you --- --- --- Wizards Model Admin › Wizards Every model job guided: new model, copy, child, split, merge, freeze, extend the metamodel, hand over, tag, archive Models Model Admin › Models, and Model hierarchy Every model you look after, and how they descend from one another The model's page Open a model Its content Grid, Data entry , views, quality, reports, KPIs, changes, history, tags, people and metamodel The metamodel The model's Metamodel tab; Model Admin › Metamodel drafts Domains, entity types, attributes, pick lists, allowed relationships and rules; drafts reviewed before they are published Quality The model's Quality tab A score, completeness, rules passed, freshness, orphans and likely duplicates, down to each entity People The model's People tab Who may do what in this model Merge requests Architecture Work › Merge requests Child models sent back to be merged, reviewed change by change Library Model Admin › Model library Reference and template models to start new models from How it is put together - A model is a set of entities a capability, an application, a node... and the relationships between them, each of a type its metamodel allows. Every entity has an ID for example APP-0012 , its attributes, its history and its links. - The metamodel says what a model may hold: domains Strategy, Business, Application, Data, Technology and so on , entity types with their attributes, relationship types and which are allowed between which types with how many , pick lists and validation rules. Every change to it is a published version with a note; children can be offered the new version Push down . - Changes are private until committed : what an Architect changes is their uncommitted change until a Committer or the Architect, when allowed commits it. Conflicts show at commit. Every commit can be rolled back. - Tags are named moments of a model, to compare with, copy from or go back to. - Families : a model can be a copy on its own or a child it keeps its parent; its changes go back as a merge request, and the parent's changes can be pushed down to it . - Model roles , highest first: Model Admin, Model Sub Admin, Committer, Architect, History Viewer, Report Viewer. Where to go next - The tasks below, one page each. - Building metamodels for a whole industry: What EA Explorer has for industry model makers industry-modeller.md ."},{"t":"What EA Explorer has for Project Admins","u":"roles/project-admin.html","s":"You run architecture projects: start them from a template, choose the ADM cycle, look after the people, deliverables, key questions and sign-off.","w":"Who this is for People with the Project Admin or Lead Architect role on a project. Project Admins look after the projects, templates and libraries of the installation under the Project Admin menu. What you have Area Where What it gives you --- --- --- Wizards Project Admin › Wizards A new project blank, from a template, or restored from a backup file and the jobs on a project Projects Project Admin › Projects Every project, its state and its people Templates and libraries Project Admin › Templates and libraries Project templates, the project content template library and the project library Principles Project Admin › Principles The organisation's architecture principles, as cards Surveys and maturity Project Admin › Surveys and maturity Questionnaires to stakeholders, and EA capability maturity assessments The project's page Open a project Its ADM wheel and phases, steps, models, deliverables and artifacts, stakeholders, key questions, principles, sign-off, documents, library and reports How it is put together - A project runs one ADM cycle or a piece of architecture work with its own people, models, deliverables and documents. It starts from one of 14 templates for example transformation, as-is documentation, build or buy, cloud migration, acquisition or blank. - The TOGAF 10 library gives the phases, steps and deliverables: 13 phases, 116 steps, 171 deliverables and artifacts, and 51 repository folders. You add your own steps and order them. - The ADM cycle is a Full cycle, one of TOGAF's iterations Architecture Capability, Development, Transition Planning, Governance or your own set of phases. Phases left out are frozen, never deleted. - Models in roles : a project uses models as its baseline, target, transition, scenario, reference or working copy, each from a tag of the model it starts from. - Documents live in the project's repository Mayan EDMS : versions, check-out, acceptance and approval. - Sign-off is by the project's sign-off people, with a quorum; decisions and dispensations go in the governance log. - Project roles : Project Admin, Lead Architect, Architect, Model Admin, Model Sub Admin and Stakeholder. Where to go next - The tasks below, one page each. - What the people on your projects can do: What EA Explorer has for users user.md ."},{"t":"What EA Explorer has for users","u":"roles/user.html","s":"You find, change, draw and report on the architecture: entities and relationships, views, reports, projects, and your own AI assistant.","w":"Who this is for Everyone who works with the architecture day to day: Architects change content , Committers review and commit changes , History Viewers and Report Viewers read and report , and the people on projects Architect , Stakeholder . What you may do depends on your roles on each model and project: what you may not use is not shown. What you have Area Where What it gives you --- --- --- Your work Architecture Work › My projects, My models The projects and models you work in, with what needs you Finding / or Ctrl+K anywhere; Me › Search everything Any function, model, project or entity by name, ID, description or value; near spellings work A model Open a model Grid a table you edit like a spreadsheet , Data entry one entity at a time in a form , Views , Quality , Reports , KPIs , Changes uncommitted , History and Tags Views A model's Views tab 49 standard views diagram, catalogue, heat map, matrix, relationships , networks, impact, capability maps, roadmaps, and drawn views in the built-in draw.io Reports A model's Reports tab 30 standard reports and dashboards, the report designer for your own, and the OData address for Power BI and Excel Compare Architecture Work › Compare and analyse Two models or two moments compared; gap analysis; common analysis across many models Projects Open a project Its phases and steps, models, deliverables, stakeholders, key questions and documents Your tasks Me › My tasks, Notifications, Surveys to answer Requests, approvals, reviews and surveys waiting for you AI AI MCP Connect your own AI assistant; it works as you, with your permissions Help ? or F1 Help for what is on the screen, every document, and this site How it is put together - Entities and relationships : every element of the architecture a capability, a process, an application, a server... is an entity of a type; relationships join them, only in the ways the metamodel allows. Each entity has an ID, attributes, links to documents, a history and the views it appears in. - Your changes are private until committed : what you add or change is your uncommitted change, seen by you and the model's Committers, until it is committed. A Committer reviews and commits it, or sends it back. - Views are drawn from the repository when you open them, so they always show the data as it is now. A drawn view you make in draw.io stays in step with the model: a relationship you draw goes into the model as your change. - History : every change is kept, so you can see any entity or model as it was at any moment or tag. Where to go next - The tasks below, one page each. - On any screen, press F1 for help with what is in front of you."},{"t":"What EA Explorer has for industry model makers","u":"roles/industry-modeller.html","s":"You build reference models and metamodels for an industry: capabilities, value streams, services, processes and a starter landscape that others start from.","w":"Who this is for People who build reference models for an industry or a domain banking, insurance, healthcare... and the metamodels they use, for others to start their own models from. You need the Model Creator role to make models, and Library Admin to publish them in the model library. What you have Area Where What it gives you --- --- --- Industry reference models Model Admin › Model library › External reference models Banking, Government, Healthcare, Logistics, Manufacturing, Minerals and Mining, Pharmaceuticals, Retail and Telecommunications, and Meridian Assurance insurance , each with capabilities, value streams, services, processes, products, business objects and a starter landscape Industry packs A reference model › Pack Each industry's book, workbook, the metamodel Excel it was built from and its empty template, ArchiMate 4 views, Excel templates and PowerPoints, to download Metamodel workbooks Model Admin › Wizards, Model from a metamodel workbook A whole metamodel as one Excel workbook: download any model's, change it, make a new model from it The metamodel editor A model's Metamodel tab Domains, types, attributes, pick lists, allowed relationships with multiplicity, rules, notation and colours Metamodel drafts Model Admin › Metamodel drafts Changes proposed, reviewed and approved before they are published Loading content A model's Import and export tab Excel and CSV sheets built for the model's own types, loaded with a preview The model library Model Admin › Model library Where a finished reference model is published for everyone to start from How it is put together - ArchiMate 4 and the TOGAF 10 content metamodel are built in, with six EA Explorer extensions for TOGAF business architecture value stream stage, product lifecycle stage, business scenario, control, contract, measure , each marked as an extension. - A metamodel workbook has one sheet each for the model's details, domains, pick lists, attributes, types, type attributes, relationship types, allowed relationships with multiplicity and rules. It is the quickest way to build or review a whole metamodel. - A reference model is an ordinary model marked as a reference and published in the library. Others copy it, or make a child of it so later changes can be pushed down to theirs. - Packs are files kept with EA Explorer and loaded into Documents at start-up, so every installation has them. Where to go next - The tasks below, one page each. - The ArchiMate and TOGAF standards themselves: Further reading ../further-reading.md ."},{"t":"What EA Explorer has for developers","u":"roles/developer.html","s":"You bring data in and take it out: the REST API, the OData feed, the published import formats, deliveries, push sources with Python, webhooks and MCP.","w":"Who this is for People who connect EA Explorer to other systems: they write the scripts and ETL jobs that send data in, read models out for reports, receive EA Explorer's events, or build on its API. EA Explorer is not an ETL tool itself: it publishes its formats and feeds, and your jobs read and write them. What you have Way in or out Where What it gives you --- --- --- The REST API /api/v1/... , described at /api/docs OpenAPI Everything the screens do Machine access System Admin › Machine access; Me › My tokens and keys Tokens, API keys and client certificates for people and service accounts, read or read-write per area, for some models or all, with an expiry The OData feed A model's Reports › OData Every entity type as a table, read only, for Power BI, Excel or any OData client Import formats A model's Import and export The Excel format and the CSV format one CSV per sheet with master.csv , empty templates made for each model Deliveries A model's Import and export › Deliveries A source per system: files dropped in its folder, sent to the API, or uploaded; previewed and accepted by a Committer Discovery sources A model's Import and export › Discovery An OData feed EA Explorer reads, a push endpoint your system sends to with a Python kit , or documents read by AI Webhooks System Admin › Settings › System settings, Webhooks IT and Super Admins Signed messages to your systems when something happens a commit, a metamodel change, a request, a model MCP AI MCP › Connect your AI assistant About 140 tools and guided prompts for an AI assistant, as the person signed in Model packages Model Admin › Wizards › Download A whole model as a zip or Excel file without data, with data, or with its history , to move between installations or put on git How it is put together - Signing in : a person signs in through Keycloak; a system uses a token or API key sent as Authorization: Bearer ... or a client certificate on the machine-access port. Each is limited to the areas and models you choose, expires, can be revoked, and every call is in the change log. - Data goes in as a delivery or a load : matched by entity type and name; a delivery only adds and changes it never deletes , and keeps EA Explorer's values unless its source's values are set to win; nothing reaches the model until a Committer accepts it. - Data comes out through the OData feed read only, with the reader's permissions , the REST API, Excel and CSV exports, and model packages. - IDs : every entity has a GUID and a display ID for example APP-0012 . Deliveries match by name, so your system does not need EA Explorer's IDs. - Permissions always apply: a token or a person reads only what they may read, and changes only what they may change. Where to go next - The tasks below, one page each. - The API's own pages in your installation: /api/docs . - The standards: OData, OpenAPI and MCP ../further-reading.md ."},{"t":"Your role","u":"roles/index.html","s":"","w":"Choose what you do with EA Explorer: each page says what the platform has for you, how it is put together, and the tasks you will do."},{"t":"Add a person and give them roles","u":"how-do-i/add-a-person-and-give-roles.html","s":"People sign in through Keycloak; their roles on the installation come from Keycloak, and their roles on each model and project are given there.","w":"Before you start You need the Keycloak Admin or User Admin role to add people, and Model Admin or Project Admin on the model or project you give roles on. Steps 1. Add the person in Keycloak or let them come from your directory, when EA Explorer signs in against it . Open https://<your EA Explorer address /auth/admin/ , choose the EA Explorer realm, then Users › Add user : their user name, name and email. Under Credentials , set a temporary password they change at their first sign-in. 2. Give them their roles on the installation , in Keycloak under Role mapping : for most people user ; for admins super-admin , it-admin , user-admin or auditor ; model-creator if they may make models; library-admin , discovery-admin or architecture-board where they need them. 3. Give them roles on a model : open the model, its People tab, then give the person a role: Model Admin, Model Sub Admin, Committer, Architect, History Viewer or Report Viewer. 4. Give them roles on a project : open the project, its People tab, then give the person a role: Project Admin, Lead Architect, Architect, Model Admin, Model Sub Admin or Stakeholder. Check it worked System Admin › Users and roles: find the person; their EA Explorer roles, projects and models are listed. They can sign in and see what their roles allow. If something goes wrong - They sign in but see almost nothing : they have no role on any model or project yet; give one steps 3 and 4 . - A directory group should give a role : map it once instead of giving the role to each person see the related page . Related - Map directory groups to roles map-directory-groups-to-roles.md - Turn on multi-factor sign-in turn-on-multi-factor-sign-in.md"},{"t":"Analyse with AI","u":"how-do-i/analyse-with-ai.html","s":"Impact, rationalisation, cost, technology risk and single points of failure, explained.","w":"Before you start Connect your AI assistant connect-your-ai-assistant.md . Things to ask - What is affected if we retire the Policy Admin system? - Which applications overlap, and what would you suggest for each? - What is the total cost by capability? - What runs on technology near its end of life, and which capabilities does that put at risk? - Where are the single points of failure? - Why did the quality score drop in September?"},{"t":"Answer key questions with views","u":"how-do-i/answer-key-questions.html","s":"The questions stakeholders ask, answered with views and accepted by the stakeholder who asked.","w":"Before you start You need a role on the project. Steps 1. The project's Stakeholders tab: add each stakeholder, their position, concerns and how you engage them. 2. The Key questions tab: + Add a key question , with who asks it. 3. Link the views that answer it, write the answer, and mark it answered. 4. The stakeholder accepts the answer it reaches them as a task . Related - Draw a view draw-a-view.md"},{"t":"Back up a project","u":"how-do-i/back-up-a-project.html","s":"A project with its documents, models and library, as one file to keep or restore.","w":"Before you start You need the Project Admin or Lead Architect role on the project. Steps 1. Open the project, its About tab, Back up and restore . 2. Back up : the file is kept with the project; download it, or Put on git . 3. To restore it, here or on another installation: Project Admin › Wizards › New project, Restore a project from a backup file . Related - Restore a backup restore-a-backup.md"},{"t":"Build a metamodel in Excel","u":"how-do-i/build-a-metamodel-in-excel.html","s":"A whole metamodel as one workbook: types, attributes, allowed relationships and rules, made into a model.","w":"Before you start You need the Model Creator role. Steps 1. Model Admin › Wizards, Model from a metamodel workbook : download the empty template, or any model's metamodel in the same layout. 2. Fill in the sheets: Model , Domains code, name, colour , Pick lists , Attributes , Types code, name, domain, ID prefix, notation, colour , Type attributes which type has which attribute, required or not , Relationship types , Allowed relationships with multiplicity: 1, 0..1, 1.. , 0.. , 2..5 and Rules . 3. Upload it and check what it would make. 4. Make a new model from it, blank the workbook is the whole metamodel , or add it to an existing model it adds and updates, never takes away . Related - Change a model's metamodel change-a-metamodel.md - Publish a reference model to the library publish-a-reference-model.md"},{"t":"Call the REST API","u":"how-do-i/call-the-rest-api.html","s":"Everything the screens do, from a script, described with OpenAPI.","w":"Before you start A token or API key see the related page . Steps 1. Open https://<your EA Explorer address /api/docs : every endpoint, what it takes and what it returns. 2. Call it with your token, for example the models you may read: curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer <token \" https://<your EA Explorer address /api/v1/models 3. Changes made through the API are yours or the service account's : uncommitted until committed, and in the change log. Related - Get a token or an API key get-a-token-or-api-key.md - Receive webhooks receive-webhooks.md"},{"t":"Change a model's metamodel","u":"how-do-i/change-a-metamodel.html","s":"Add or change entity types, attributes, pick lists, allowed relationships and rules, reviewed before they are published.","w":"Before you start You need the Model Admin role on the model. Steps 1. Open the model, its Metamodel tab: domains, entity types, attributes, pick lists, relationship types, allowed relationships with how many: 1, 0..1, 1.. , 0.. and rules. 2. Make the change. A change that needs a review waits as a metamodel draft Model Admin › Metamodel drafts : others comment, then it is approved or rejected. 3. Approved, it is published as a new version with its note; any two versions can be compared. 4. Push down : offer the new version to the model's children Model Admin › Wizards, Propagate to a child . To take a whole set of types from another model: Model Admin › Wizards, Extend from another model . Check it worked The Metamodel tab shows the new version; data entry and the import sheets offer the new types and attributes. Related - Build a metamodel in Excel build-a-metamodel-in-excel.md"},{"t":"Change content and commit it","u":"how-do-i/change-content-and-commit.html","s":"Add and change entities and relationships, then commit them so everyone sees them.","w":"Before you start You need the Architect role or higher on the model; committing needs Committer. Steps 1. Open the model. Change content in the Grid a table: click a cell to edit; copy and paste from Excel or in Data entry one entity at a time in a form: choose a type, then + New or open an entity . 2. Add relationships on the entity's Relations, or draw them in a drawn view; only the relationships the metamodel allows are offered. 3. Your changes are uncommitted : only you and the model's Committers see them. The Changes tab lists them. 4. Commit with a message saying what and why for example October figures added . If you are not a Committer, a Committer reviews and commits them, or sends them back. If something goes wrong - A clash : someone committed a change to the same thing after you started. For each clash choose yours or theirs. - Undo a commit : the model's History, the commit, Roll back a new commit that puts things back . Related - Load data from Excel load-data-from-excel.md"},{"t":"Change content with AI","u":"how-do-i/change-content-with-ai.html","s":"Your AI assistant adds and changes entities and relationships as your uncommitted changes.","w":"Before you start Connect your AI assistant connect-your-ai-assistant.md . You need the Architect role or higher on the model. Things to ask - Read this strategy and create the drivers, goals and outcomes with their links. - Load this table of applications into the model. - Give every application without an owner the owner of its capability. - Make a copy of this model and remove all duplicates as you see fit. What happens It shows the changes first and makes them only after your yes. They are your uncommitted changes until committed, like any other; the model is tagged first."},{"t":"Check the health and alerts","u":"how-do-i/check-health-and-alerts.html","s":"See whether every part of EA Explorer is up, what is wrong, and who is told.","w":"Before you start You need the Super Admin, IT Admin or Auditor role. Steps 1. The dot in the top bar shows the overall health at a glance: green, amber or red. 2. System Admin › Running › Health : every part the API, the databases, sign-in, reports, documents and the rest ; open a red one to see why. 3. System Admin › Running › Alerts : the checks that run every minute each service, the disks, memory, the certificate, the database, errors in the web log, the self-test and the open alerts. Alerts go to the IT Admins and Super Admins, the webhooks and by email. 4. Acknowledge an alert to stop it repeating, or silence a check during planned work. On the machine: eax status shows every container, the disks and what is running. If something goes wrong - A service keeps restarting : System Admin › Running › Containers, the service, its log. - Everything is down : on the machine, eax status , then eax restart . Related - Run the self-test run-the-self-test.md"},{"t":"Choose the project's ADM cycle","u":"how-do-i/choose-the-adm-cycle.html","s":"A full ADM cycle, one of TOGAF's iterations, or your own set of phases.","w":"Before you start You need a role on the project. Steps 1. Open the project. On its page, choose the cycle: Full cycle , one of TOGAF's iterations Architecture Capability , Development , Transition Planning , Governance , or Custom the phases you tick . 2. Phases left out are frozen on the ADM wheel and the phase tabs: read only, never deleted. Choose again at any time. 3. In each phase, tick steps as they are done and add your own; put them in your own order. Related - Track deliverables and sign-off track-deliverables-and-sign-off.md"},{"t":"Compare two models or two moments","u":"how-do-i/compare-two-models.html","s":"What was added, changed and removed between two models, or one model at two tags.","w":"Steps 1. Architecture Work › Compare and analyse › Compare models . 2. Choose two models, or one model at two tags. 3. Read what was added, changed and removed, type by type; open any entity. 4. Gap analysis same menu between a baseline and a target, with resolutions and work packages; Common analysis across many models. Related - Tag a model and compare tag-and-compare.md"},{"t":"Connect your AI assistant","u":"how-do-i/connect-your-ai-assistant.html","s":"Your own AI app talks to EA Explorer through MCP, as you, with your permissions.","w":"Before you start MCP is switched on in your installation System Admin › Settings › System settings , and your AI app can use MCP connectors. Steps 1. Open AI MCP › Connect your AI assistant and copy the address. 2. In your AI app's connector settings, add it. When the browser asks, sign in to EA Explorer as yourself. 3. Ask something simple: list the models I can see . What to know - It works as you : it reads only what you may read and changes only what you may change. - Anything that changes something is shown first and done only after your yes ; the model is tagged first. - Every call is in AI MCP › My AI activity . - AI MCP › What it can do lists everything it can do, as tiles. Related - Explore a model with AI explore-a-model-with-ai.md"},{"t":"Create a model","u":"how-do-i/create-a-model.html","s":"A new model: blank on a metamodel, a copy of another, a child that merges back, or started from a library model.","w":"Before you start You need the Model Creator role to make a model from nothing, or Model Admin on the model you copy. Steps 1. Open Model Admin › Wizards , then choose: - New model : blank, on the metamodel you choose ArchiMate 4, TOGAF 10, an industry's, or your own . - Copy a model from the library : start from a reference or template model. - Copy with the parent-child link : a child; its work merges back, and the parent's metamodel changes flow down. - Copy without the link : a separate copy, with or without the data. 2. Give it a name and say who looks after it. Every wizard asks before it changes anything. 3. Open the new model and give people their roles on its People tab. Check it worked The model is listed on Model Admin › Models and in Model hierarchy, under its parent if it has one. Related - Give people roles on a model give-people-roles-on-a-model.md - Build a metamodel in Excel build-a-metamodel-in-excel.md"},{"t":"Discover the enterprise with AI","u":"how-do-i/discover-the-enterprise-with-ai.html","s":"Your AI assistant reads your sources and proposes what it finds for a model.","w":"Before you start A Discovery Admin has set up a discovery project AI MCP › Enterprise discovery with its target model and sources. Steps 1. Ask your AI assistant to run the discovery project. 2. It reads the sources mailboxes, folders, SharePoint, Git, wikis, ticket systems, database schemas and more and proposes the elements and relationships it finds, each with where it was found. 3. What it proposes is reviewed like any change. Documents marked NOT FOR AI USE are never read."},{"t":"Draw a view","u":"how-do-i/draw-a-view.html","s":"A view drawn in the built-in draw.io with the model's own entities, kept in step with the model.","w":"Before you start You need a role on the model; drawing relationships into the model needs Architect or higher. Steps 1. Open the model, its Views tab. Start a new drawn view name it; it opens in its own tab , or open any picture a network, a capability map, a standard view and Save as a drawn view . 2. Drag entities in from the search panel; the shapes use the ArchiMate 4 notation. A shape can be a placeholder until the entity exists. 3. Lines you draw between entities go into the model as your change, only the relationship types the metamodel allows. Deleting a line asks: hide it in the view, or delete it from the model. 4. Notes, comments and arrows from draw.io's general shapes never touch the model. 5. Save: each save is kept as a version. Export as PNG, SVG, PDF or .drawio. Related - Open a report or a view open-a-report-or-view.md"},{"t":"Explore a model with AI","u":"how-do-i/explore-a-model-with-ai.html","s":"Ask your AI assistant about a model: what is in it, how things relate, what changed.","w":"Before you start Connect your AI assistant connect-your-ai-assistant.md . Things to ask - What applications support the claims capability in the Meridian model? - Show me everything within two steps of the Policy Admin system. - What changed in this model since the Baseline 2026 tag? - Which entities have no relationships? The answers carry links back to the entities, so you can open them in EA Explorer."},{"t":"Find and merge duplicates","u":"how-do-i/find-and-merge-duplicates.html","s":"Entities that are the same thing under close names, found and merged into one, their relationships moved to it.","w":"Before you start You need a role that may change the model. Steps 1. Open the model, Quality › Duplicates . 2. Choose an entity type type a few letters to find it and how close the names must be. Tick attributes to match on as well, for example Vendor and Version. 3. Find duplicates . Download the result with Excel , or open a group with Compare and merge . 4. Choose the entity kept and each field's value; relationships move to it, and its old IDs still find it. 5. Commit, as any change. Related - Check and improve data quality improve-data-quality.md"},{"t":"Find anything","u":"how-do-i/find-anything.html","s":"Any function, model, project or entity, by name, ID, description or value.","w":"Steps 1. Press / or Ctrl+K anywhere, and type. It finds functions every menu item, with where it is , the page's tabs and actions, help pages, and content models, projects, entities as you type. Near spellings work. 2. For a search across every model you can read, with filters: Me › Search everything . 3. Right-click any entity a row, a card, a link to open it, edit it, see its graph, history or related entities, or add it to a view. Related - Get help on any screen get-help-on-any-screen.md"},{"t":"Get a token or an API key","u":"how-do-i/get-a-token-or-api-key.html","s":"A credential for a script or another system, limited to what it needs.","w":"Before you start Your own token: any signed-in person. A service account's API key or a client certificate: an IT Admin or Super Admin. Steps 1. Your own: Me › My tokens and keys . For a system: System Admin › Machine access . 2. New token : choose the areas read or read-write per API area , optionally only some models or projects, and an expiry. 3. Copy the secret: it is shown once. 4. Send it with every call as Authorization: Bearer <token . A client certificate, trusted on the same page, signs in on the machine-access port instead. Check it worked Machine access shows when each was last used; every call is in the change log. If something goes wrong - Revoke it at once if it leaks; make a new one. Related - Call the REST API call-the-rest-api.md"},{"t":"Get an administrator back in","u":"how-do-i/get-an-administrator-back-in.html","s":"A forgotten password, a locked account or a lost phone, sorted from the machine.","w":"Before you start You need to be on the machine EA Explorer runs on. This is only for the administrators; everyone else is helped by an administrator in Keycloak. Steps 1. eax access admins lists the administrators, and whether each is enabled. 2. A forgotten password : eax access reset-password <user name gives a temporary password, shown once; it must be changed at the next sign-in. 3. Locked out after wrong passwords : eax access unlock <user name . 4. A lost phone : eax access mfa-off <user name removes the authenticator; a new one is set up at the next sign-in. 5. Sign-in itself is down : the break-glass page / /break-glass signs in with the break-glass password, kept offline by the Super Admins. Related - Install and run: A forgotten password or certificate ../install/forgotten.html"},{"t":"Get help on any screen","u":"how-do-i/get-help-on-any-screen.html","s":"What the screen in front of you is for, and how to use it.","w":"Steps 1. Press F1 , or ? › Help for this page: a panel beside the page explains what is on the screen the pop-up, the wizard step, the tab or the page , with a search over all the help. 2. Hover over a button, tab or field for a short tooltip. 3. ? › Documentation: every document that ships with your version, each printable. 4. This website: ? › Website, with every How do I page and the role guides. Related - Find anything find-anything.md"},{"t":"Give people roles on a model","u":"how-do-i/give-people-roles-on-a-model.html","s":"Who may read, change, commit and look after one model.","w":"Before you start You need the Model Admin role on the model. Steps 1. Open the model, its People tab. 2. Give a person a role, highest first: - Model Admin : everything on the model, including its metamodel and people. - Model Sub Admin : helps the Model Admin; reviews deliveries. - Committer : reviews and commits changes. - Architect : changes content as uncommitted changes . - History Viewer : reads the model and its history. - Report Viewer : reads reports. 3. Take a role away when it is no longer needed. To hand the model over to new Model Admins: Model Admin › Wizards, Hand over . Related - Add a person and give them roles add-a-person-and-give-roles.md"},{"t":"Check and improve data quality","u":"how-do-i/improve-data-quality.html","s":"See how complete, correct and current a model is, and fix what it finds.","w":"Before you start You need a role on the model; fixing needs Architect or higher. Steps 1. Open the model, its Quality tab: a score, completeness, rules passed, freshness, orphans and likely duplicates. 2. Open any tile to see the entities behind it. 3. Model Admin › Wizards, Improve data quality walks through what it finds one entity at a time: fill in, not applicable, or still correct. 4. Commit the changes the Changes tab . Check it worked The score rises as changes are committed. The KPIs tab keeps the score month by month. Related - Find and merge duplicates find-and-merge-duplicates.md"},{"t":"Limit who can reach EA Explorer","u":"how-do-i/limit-who-can-reach-ea-explorer.html","s":"IP allow lists: only the addresses you list may reach EA Explorer, its sign-in pages, System Admin, the AI connector or the machine port.","w":"Before you start You need the Super Admin or IT Admin role, and the addresses or ranges your people come from for example the office's 10.20.0.0/16 . Steps 1. Open System Admin › Security , Allowed addresses . 2. Each place has its own list: site everything , signin the sign-in pages , admin System Admin , mcp the AI connector and machine the client-certificate port . An empty list lets everyone in. 3. Add an address or range with a name and why, then Save . It applies at once, without a restart. Check it worked From an address not on the list, the place answers with a refusal. System Admin › Security shows the addresses refused. If something goes wrong - A change that would shut you out is refused on the screen, so you cannot lock yourself out. - Everyone is locked out anyway for example the office's address changed : on the machine, eax allow clear empties every list, or eax allow add site <address lets one in. The machine itself and EA Explorer's own containers are always allowed. Related - Turn on multi-factor sign-in turn-on-multi-factor-sign-in.md"},{"t":"Load data from Excel","u":"how-do-i/load-data-from-excel.html","s":"Download a sheet built for the model, fill it in, upload it and check the preview.","w":"Before you start You need the Architect role or higher on the model. Steps 1. Open the model, Import and export or Model Admin › Wizards, Load data . 2. Choose the entity types and download the sheet: one sheet per type with drop-downs, and a Relationships sheet. 3. Fill it in. Leave the IDs as they are for rows already there; new rows need a name. 4. Upload it. A preview shows the new, changed and problem rows before anything loads. 5. Load: the rows become your uncommitted changes. Commit them. If something goes wrong - The preview names each problem row and why a value not in the pick list, a relationship the metamodel does not allow . - Undo a whole load on its load page. Related - Change content and commit it change-content-and-commit.md - Send data with a delivery send-data-with-a-delivery.md"},{"t":"Look after the installation with AI","u":"how-do-i/look-after-the-installation-with-ai.html","s":"For admins: ask about the installation's state, usage and housekeeping.","w":"Before you start Connect your AI assistant connect-your-ai-assistant.md . You need the Super Admin or IT Admin role. Things to ask - How is the installation? Is anything slowing it down? - Which models haven't been used this quarter? - Run a housekeeping dry run and explain it. - Track the number of applications on an unsupported operating system. Making credentials, roles or service accounts stays in the screens, never through the AI."},{"t":"Map directory groups to roles","u":"how-do-i/map-directory-groups-to-roles.html","s":"Make a Keycloak role or a directory group give an EA Explorer role, so people get their roles from the groups they are already in.","w":"Before you start You need the User Admin or Super Admin role. Your directory Active Directory or another LDAP, or your identity provider is connected to Keycloak. Steps 1. Open System Admin › Users and roles › Keycloak role mapping . 2. Choose the Keycloak role or directory group, and the EA Explorer global role it gives for example the group EA-Architects gives user , EA-Admins gives it-admin . 3. Add . The mapping applies at each person's next sign-in. Check it worked A person in that group signs in again; System Admin › Users and roles shows the role on them, with where it came from. If something goes wrong - Nothing changed for the person : they must sign out and in again. Check the group name is exactly as Keycloak sees it. - To take a mapping away : Remove beside it; people keep any role given to them directly. Related - Add a person and give them roles add-a-person-and-give-roles.md"},{"t":"Merge a child model back","u":"how-do-i/merge-a-child-model-back.html","s":"A child's changes sent to its parent, reviewed change by change, and merged as one commit.","w":"Before you start You need Model Admin on the child to send, and Model Admin or Committer on the parent to review. Steps 1. On the child: Model Admin › Wizards, Send for merge into the parent . It shows what changed since its starting point; add a note and send. 2. On the parent: Architecture Work › Merge requests , open the request. Where both changed the same thing, it is a conflict. 3. Accept or reject each change a reason for each rejection , then merge it as one commit. A merge report can be downloaded in Word. 4. Then the child is frozen, or refreshed from the parent to carry on. Related - Tag a model and compare tag-and-compare.md"},{"t":"Copy settings to another site","u":"how-do-i/move-settings-between-sites.html","s":"Export the admin settings to a file, and import them on another site, with every difference shown first.","w":"Before you start You need the Super Admin role on both sites. Steps 1. On the first site: System Admin › Settings › Settings import and export . Tick the parts for example system settings, branding, alerts, schedules and Export to a file , or Put on git . 2. On the other site, the same page: Choose a settings file or From git . 3. Every difference is shown: the value here and in the file. Nothing changes yet. 4. Tick what to take, then Take . A safety copy of the settings there is kept first, and each change goes in the audit trail. On the machine: eax settings export <file and eax settings import <file it shows the differences; add --yes to take them . Check it worked The page says how many were taken. The safety copy is listed below. If something goes wrong - Undo on the safety copy puts the settings back as they were. - Passwords, keys, certificates, people and content never travel in the file. Related - Set up a DR site set-up-a-dr-site.md"},{"t":"Open a report or a view","u":"how-do-i/open-a-report-or-view.html","s":"The standard views and reports, your own, and the model's KPIs.","w":"Steps 1. Open the model, its Views tab: the 49 standard views, each as a diagram, catalogue, heat map, matrix and relationship list, and the drawn views. 2. Its Reports tab: the standard reports and dashboards, the Report designer for your own a type, its columns, related types and filters , and the OData address for Power BI and Excel. 3. Its KPIs tab: the model's key figures month by month and at every tag. 4. Click any box in a picture to open the entity. Related - Read a model in Power BI or Excel read-a-model-in-power-bi-or-excel.md"},{"t":"Plan a project with AI","u":"how-do-i/plan-a-project-with-ai.html","s":"An ADM project planned from a template, scenarios compared, a change checked against principles.","w":"Before you start Connect your AI assistant connect-your-ai-assistant.md . Things to ask - Plan an ADM project for the claims transformation, from the transformation template. - Make a scenario where we replace the Policy Admin system with the new platform, and show the impact. - Check this proposed change against our principles and standards. - Summarise the conflicts in this merge request and suggest a decision for each."},{"t":"Publish a reference model to the library","u":"how-do-i/publish-a-reference-model.html","s":"Your finished model in the model library, for everyone to start from.","w":"Before you start Promoting needs Model Admin on the model; publishing needs the Library Admin role. Steps 1. Model Admin › Wizards on the model, Promote to the library : a copy becomes a library model, a draft. 2. Request publishing . 3. A Library Admin opens it: Approve and publish , send it back, or reject it. 4. Published, it is listed in the model library; anyone may copy it or make a child of it. To take it out later: Withdraw from the library and restore it . Related - Build a metamodel in Excel build-a-metamodel-in-excel.md"},{"t":"Push data with Python","u":"how-do-i/push-data-with-python.html","s":"A push source and the Python kit: your records sent in one call, proposed as a delivery.","w":"Before you start Someone who may change the model sets up a push source on its Import and export › Discovery tab. Steps 1. On the push source's panel, Push with Python , then Download the Python kit zip : push to eax.py , requirements.txt pandas and requests , a README.md and sample CSV files for every type of the model. 2. Set up Python as the README says a venv , and try the samples. 3. Your own job sends its records: push dataframe url, df, username, password for one set, push dataframes for several related sets go together, so their links become relationships . Sign in with a user name and password, or a token. 4. What arrives is proposed as a delivery, previewed and accepted by a Committer. Related - Send data with a delivery send-data-with-a-delivery.md"},{"t":"Put in your organisation's certificate","u":"how-do-i/put-in-your-certificate.html","s":"Replace the self-made certificate with your organisation's, so browsers trust EA Explorer without a warning.","w":"Before you start You need the Super Admin or IT Admin role, and a certificate covering the name people open for example ea.example.org , reports. and docs. before it, with its private key no password and the chain. Steps 1. Open System Admin › Running › Secrets , Front door certificate . 2. Upload the certificate, the chain and the key. It is checked first: the names it covers, its dates, that the key matches, that the chain is complete. 3. It is used at once, with no restart and nobody signed out. The one before is kept to undo. On the machine: eax certs front install --cert <certificate file --key <key file --chain <chain file ; eax certs front shows the one in use; eax certs front undo puts the one before back. Check it worked Open EA Explorer in a browser: the padlock shows your organisation's certificate, with no warning. If something goes wrong - Refused : the message says why a name it does not cover, a key that does not match, a missing chain . - Expiry : alerts come 30 days before it ends and on the day. Related - Install and run: Real certificates ../install/certificates.html , where you give your file names and get the commands filled in."},{"t":"Put up a banner","u":"how-do-i/put-up-a-banner.html","s":"One short message under the top bar for everyone, or for admins only, with optional start and end times.","w":"Before you start You need the Super Admin or IT Admin role. Steps 1. Open System Admin › Settings › Banner . 2. Write the message, choose the level information, notice or urgent , who sees it everyone or admins only , and if you like a link and the times it shows. 3. Save : it shows at once, and starts and ends by itself. 4. Clear to show nothing. Related - Schedule a command schedule-a-command.md"},{"t":"Read a model in Power BI or Excel","u":"how-do-i/read-a-model-in-power-bi-or-excel.html","s":"The model's OData feed: every entity type as a table, read only, with your permissions.","w":"Steps 1. Open the model, Reports › OData , and copy the address https://<your EA Explorer address /api/v1/odata/models/<model id / . 2. Excel : Data › Get Data › From Other Sources › OData feed; paste the address. Power BI : Get data › OData feed. 3. Sign in with Basic : your EA Explorer user name and password, or your user name and a token as the password the way for single sign-on users . 4. Choose the entity types tables and load. Related - Get a token or an API key get-a-token-or-api-key.md"},{"t":"Receive webhooks","u":"how-do-i/receive-webhooks.html","s":"Signed messages to your system when something happens in EA Explorer.","w":"Before you start An IT Admin or Super Admin adds the webhook. Steps 1. System Admin › Settings › System settings , Webhooks : Add webhook with your address and the kinds it receives commits, metamodel changes, requests, models; none ticked means all . 2. EA Explorer sends each event as JSON to your address, signed: check the X-EAX-Signature header HMAC-SHA256 of the body with the webhook's secret before trusting it. 3. Each delivery and its answer is kept, so failed ones can be seen. Related - Call the REST API call-the-rest-api.md"},{"t":"Restore a backup","u":"how-do-i/restore-a-backup.html","s":"Put back a model, a project, part of the installation or all of it, from a backup.","w":"Before you start Restoring the installation needs the Super Admin or IT Admin role; a model needs its Model Admin; a project its Project Admin. Take a backup first, so you can go back. Careful Restoring the whole installation puts back everything as it was at the backup: work done since is lost. EA Explorer is read only while it runs. Steps 1. A model : Model Admin › Wizards on the model, Restore a tag , or its backups to restore it over itself or as a new model. 2. A project : the project's About tab, Back up and restore . 3. Part of the installation the databases, the files or the config : System Admin › Backups and restores › Backups, the backup, Restore , and choose the part. On the machine: eax restore <backup --what db . 4. Everything : the same, choosing everything. On the machine: eax restore <backup --what full . Check it worked System Admin › Backups and restores › Restores shows each restore and its log. After a restore the database integrity check runs by itself System Admin › Running › Database maintenance . If something goes wrong - Read the restore's log on the Restores page; it says which step stopped and why. - eax status on the machine shows every container; eax restart brings them up again. Related - Take a backup and check it take-and-check-a-backup.md - Install and run: Restores ../install/restores.html"},{"t":"Rotate passwords and keys","u":"how-do-i/rotate-passwords-and-keys.html","s":"Change EA Explorer's own passwords and keys, one at a time or all at once, now or on a schedule.","w":"Before you start You need the Super Admin or IT Admin role. Rotation is off until you choose it. Steps 1. Open System Admin › Running › Secrets . Every password, key and certificate is listed by name never its value , with its age and when it is next due. The yellow box says what needs a person, and why. 2. Rotate now beside one changes it at once; the services that use it start again in a few seconds. 3. Rotate all changes every one together, behind the maintenance page it asks first , then asks you to restart. 4. Rotate all regularly monthly or every three months or once at a time , from the same page. On the machine: eax secrets show , eax secrets rotate <name , eax secrets rotate --all --restart . Check it worked The age of each rotated one starts again; sign in and open Reports and Documents. If something goes wrong - On Windows, rotation that remakes services runs from PowerShell on the machine eax secrets rotate --all --restart . - eax restart takes down a maintenance page left behind and starts everything again. Related - Get an administrator back in get-an-administrator-back-in.md"},{"t":"Run a survey or a maturity assessment","u":"how-do-i/run-a-survey.html","s":"Questions to stakeholders through their task list, and EA capability maturity assessed and scored.","w":"Before you start Surveys need the Project Admin role; maturity assessments need a Super Admin. Steps 1. Project Admin › Surveys and maturity › Surveys : a designer with sections, eight kinds of question and conditions. 2. Send it to people, global roles, models or projects: it reaches them in their task list and by a link, with reminders and a closing date; it can be anonymous. 3. Results by question, downloadable as Excel. Answers never change a model. 4. EA capability maturity : assessments on nine architecture elements and six levels, scored per element and overall, with targets and gaps, and a trend over assessments. Related - Use AI for surveys use-ai-for-surveys.md"},{"t":"Run the self-test","u":"how-do-i/run-the-self-test.html","s":"Check the installation works: the smoke test in a few minutes, or the full test.","w":"Before you start You need the Super Admin or IT Admin role. Steps 1. Open System Admin › Tools › Self-test . 2. Smoke test : every role signs in, every main area answers, every page opens and the key journeys work once a few minutes . Full test : every API endpoint as every role, the database, security, and every page and journey in a browser. 3. Start it. It makes its own test data, tests, writes a report and removes what it made; nothing else changes. On the machine: eax test smoke or eax test full . Check it worked The run ends Passed . Its History entry has the report; each failure says what was asked and what came back. If something goes wrong - Run the failed ones again : History, the run, or eax test failed : only what failed, showing each check then and now. Related - Check the health and alerts check-health-and-alerts.md"},{"t":"Schedule a command","u":"how-do-i/schedule-a-command.html","s":"An eax command that runs by itself: a nightly backup, a weekly check, or once at a time.","w":"Before you start You need the Super Admin or IT Admin role. Steps 1. Open System Admin › Tools › Command centre , Schedules . 2. New schedule : choose the command and its options, then when it runs: every night, every week, every hour, once, or a cron line. Times are in the installation's time zone. 3. A command that deletes everything needs a Super Admin and the installation's name, once, when the schedule is made. 4. Turn a schedule off and on, run it now, or remove it. Every run is in the History. Check it worked The schedule shows its next run; after it runs, its last result. Related - Take a backup and check it take-and-check-a-backup.md"},{"t":"Send data with a delivery","u":"how-do-i/send-data-with-a-delivery.html","s":"Your system writes the published Excel or CSV format; EA Explorer previews it for a Committer to accept.","w":"Before you start The model's Model Admin has set up a delivery source for your system. Steps 1. Get the empty template: the model's Import and export , choose the types, tick Empty template , Excel or CSV set. It has exactly the columns and drop-down values the model accepts. 2. Write your data in it. Rows are matched by type and name : an existing entity of that type and name is updated, otherwise a new one is made. A delivery never deletes. 3. Deliver it, one of three ways: - A folder : drop the files in the source's incoming folder, then Take dropped files or eax import <source . - The API , as the source's service account: curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer <token \" -F file=@cmdb.zip https://<your EA Explorer address /api/v1/import-sources/<source id /deliveries - An upload on the Deliveries tab. 4. It waits for review: a Committer accepts or declines it. Related - Set up a delivery source set-up-a-delivery-source.md - Push data with Python push-data-with-python.md"},{"t":"Set up a delivery source","u":"how-do-i/set-up-a-delivery-source.html","s":"Another system sends its data to a model as deliveries, each previewed and accepted by a Committer.","w":"Before you start You need Model Admin on the model. For a system that sends through the API, a service account with a token System Admin › Machine access . Steps 1. Open the model, Import and export › Deliveries . 2. Add a source : its name, its folder, whether its values win over EA Explorer's, who is told, and optionally the service account that sends it. 3. The system then sends deliveries in the Excel or CSV format, by a folder, the API or an upload see the related page . 4. Each delivery is previewed new, changed, kept, unchanged, problems and waits. A Committer, Model Sub Admin or Model Admin accepts it committed as their load, undone like any load or declines it. Related - Send data with a delivery send-data-with-a-delivery.md - Push data with Python push-data-with-python.md"},{"t":"Set up a DR site","u":"how-do-i/set-up-a-dr-site.html","s":"A second EA Explorer kept up to date with this one, read only, ready to take over.","w":"Before you start You need the Super Admin role on both sites, and a second installation of the same release see Install and run: A server . Steps 1. On the DR site : System Admin › Running › Site pairings, Make a key . It is shown once: copy it. 2. On this site : the same page, Pair with a site : the DR site's address, the key, and DR sync . 3. On the DR site : accept the pairing. It becomes read only and is kept up to date by itself. 4. Rehearse now and then with the restore drill System Admin › Backups and restores › Disaster recovery . Check it worked Both sites show the pairing as paired; the batches list what was sent and committed. If the primary is lost On the DR site: the DR pairing, Stop and take over . Then point the name people open at the DR site. Related - Install and run: A DR site ../install/dr-site.html - Install and run: Switching to DR and back ../install/switch-to-dr.html"},{"t":"Start an architecture project","u":"how-do-i/start-an-architecture-project.html","s":"A new project from one of the templates or blank, with its models, people and ADM cycle.","w":"Before you start You need the Project Admin role. Steps 1. Open Project Admin › Wizards › New project : Blank project , From a project template… , or Restore a project from a backup file . 2. A template transformation, as-is documentation, build or buy, cloud migration, acquisition and others sets the phases, steps, deliverables and the models' roles. 3. Choose the base : the models the project starts from and the tag each is taken at. 4. Give people their roles on the project's People tab: Project Admin, Lead Architect, Architect, Model Admin, Model Sub Admin or Stakeholder. Check it worked The project opens on its ADM wheel; Architecture Work › My projects lists it for everyone on it. Related - Choose the project's ADM cycle choose-the-adm-cycle.md"},{"t":"Tag a model and compare","u":"how-do-i/tag-and-compare.html","s":"A named moment of a model to go back to, and what changed since.","w":"Before you start Tagging needs Model Admin on the model; comparing needs a role on both models. Steps 1. Tag it : Model Admin › Wizards, Tag it now , with a name for example Baseline 2026 . Every wizard that changes a model tags it first. 2. Compare : Architecture Work › Compare and analyse › Compare models : two models, or one model at two tags. It shows what was added, changed and removed. 3. Gap analysis : the same menu, Gap analysis , between a baseline and a target, with resolutions and work packages. 4. Go back : the model's Tags tab, Restore a tag makes it the latest again. Related - Merge a child model back merge-a-child-model-back.md"},{"t":"Take a backup and check it","u":"how-do-i/take-and-check-a-backup.html","s":"A backup of the whole installation now, and a check that it restores, without touching what is live.","w":"Before you start You need the Super Admin or IT Admin role. Careful A backup puts the maintenance page up for a few minutes and waits for background work to finish first, so everything in it is from one moment. The screen asks before it starts. Steps 1. Open System Admin › Backups and restores › Backups . 2. Back up now , with a tag that says why for example before-upgrade . Or on the machine: eax backup before-upgrade . 3. When it is done, it is listed with its size. Pin it to keep it for good pinned backups are never removed . 4. Check it restores: on the machine, eax verify restores the newest backup into scratch copies and compares; nothing live is touched. Check it worked The backup is listed, newest first, and its log ends without errors. eax backups lists them on the machine. If something goes wrong - It waits a long time at the start : something in the background is still running; the backup waits up to 30 minutes, then goes ahead and says what was still busy. System Admin › Running › Jobs shows what is running. - Keep a copy off this machine : a DR pack eax dr-pack <folder holds everything needed to rebuild elsewhere. Related - Restore a backup restore-a-backup.md - Install and run: Backups ../install/backups.html"},{"t":"Track deliverables and sign-off","u":"how-do-i/track-deliverables-and-sign-off.html","s":"The project's documents and artifacts, their versions, and their approval by the sign-off people.","w":"Before you start You need a role on the project. Steps 1. The project's Deliverables and artifacts tab lists what the project produces; open one to see it, its versions and its sign-off. 2. Documents live in the project's repository: check out, change, check in as a new version. 3. The Sign-off tab lists what is waiting: the sign-off people approve, reject or record a decision with evidence, with a quorum where one is set. 4. Decisions and dispensations go in the governance log. Related - Answer key questions with views answer-key-questions.md"},{"t":"Turn on multi-factor sign-in","u":"how-do-i/turn-on-multi-factor-sign-in.html","s":"Ask admins, or everyone, for a one-time code from an authenticator app when they sign in.","w":"Before you start You need the Super Admin or IT Admin role. People need an authenticator app on their phone. Steps 1. Open System Admin › Security . 2. Under Multi-factor sign-in , choose Admins the Super Admins and IT Admins or Everyone . Off is the default. 3. Save. It applies at once: the people it covers set up their authenticator at their next sign-in. Check it worked Sign out and in: after the password, EA Explorer asks for the code the first time, it shows a QR code to scan . If something goes wrong - Someone lost their phone : on System Admin › Security, reset their authenticator; they set up a new one at the next sign-in. An administrator locked out can be helped from the machine: eax access mfa-off <user name . Related - Get an administrator back in get-an-administrator-back-in.md - Limit who can reach EA Explorer limit-who-can-reach-ea-explorer.md"},{"t":"Update to a new release","u":"how-do-i/update-to-a-new-release.html","s":"Move EA Explorer to a newer release, with a full backup first and a way back.","w":"Before you start You need the Super Admin or IT Admin role. Read the release's notes: they say what changes and anything to do before. Steps 1. Open System Admin › Updates . It shows the version installed and the newer releases offered, each with its notes. 2. Choose the release and Update now , or at a time a banner tells people beforehand . 3. EA Explorer takes a pinned full backup first, then moves one release at a time. On the machine: eax update --list shows what is offered; eax update moves to the newest. Check it worked The version at the top left of every screen changes; everyone sees What's new once. Run the smoke test System Admin › Tools › Self-test, or eax test smoke . If something goes wrong - A failed step stops and asks: Retry or Roll back . On the machine: eax rollback goes back to the release before, with its data as it was. Related - Run the self-test run-the-self-test.md - Releases ../releases/index.html"},{"t":"Use AI for surveys","u":"how-do-i/use-ai-for-surveys.html","s":"A survey made from plain words, sent and summarised.","w":"Before you start Connect your AI assistant connect-your-ai-assistant.md . Things to ask - Ask the architects how they use the repository, five questions. - Send it and remind those who have not answered. - Summarise the results."},{"t":"Use an industry pack","u":"how-do-i/use-an-industry-pack.html","s":"Start from an industry's reference model, and download its book, workbook and templates.","w":"Steps 1. Model Admin › Model library › External reference models : Banking, Government, Healthcare, Logistics, Manufacturing, Minerals and Mining, Pharmaceuticals, Retail, Telecommunications, and Meridian Assurance insurance . 2. Open one; its Pack tab has the industry's files as tiles: the book, the workbook, the metamodel Excel it was built from and its empty template, ArchiMate 4 views, Excel templates and PowerPoints. Download any of them. 3. To start your own model from it: Model Admin › Wizards, Copy a model from the library or make a child, so later changes to the reference model can come down to yours . If something goes wrong - A tile says not loaded : a Library Admin clicks Load packs from the folder on the server , or runs eax packs load on the machine. Related - Create a model create-a-model.md"},{"t":"Write a report or a deck with AI","u":"how-do-i/write-a-report-with-ai.html","s":"A document or a presentation from a model or a project, with links to its sources.","w":"Before you start Connect your AI assistant connect-your-ai-assistant.md . Things to ask - Write a current-state summary of the claims domain as a Word document in the project. - Write an executive summary of this gap analysis. - Make a ten-slide deck on this project: its outline, key views and decisions. The document is saved in the project for review; a deck's views come as pictures or data from EA Explorer."},{"t":"How do I","u":"how-do-i/index.html","s":"","w":"One task on each page, step by step, ready to print or save as PDF. Choose your role, or type to find a task."},{"t":"Install and run","u":"install/index.html","s":"","w":"Each guide is guided three ways: System Admin Setup, eax setup <guide and a Jenkins pipeline R6.6, D750 . Windows: .\\eax . macOS and Linux: ./eax.sh . Guide What it is for --- --- A laptop laptop.md EA Explorer on your own computer, to try it or to work alone A server server.md EA Explorer for a team, on a Linux server with Docker Any server over SSH remote.md EA Explorer put on another machine from this one no cloud-specific code, D746 A new machine new-machine.md A machine made ready for EA Explorer: Docker, disk, folders, network Backups backups.md What is backed up, when, where to keep it, and checking it works Restores restores.md A model, a project, a part or everything put back A catastrophic failure catastrophe.md The machine or its data is lost: what to do first, who to tell, what to check Building an environment from a backup rebuild.md A new machine made from a backup or a DR pack, nothing lost A DR site dr-site.md A second site kept up to date, ready to take over Switching to DR and back switch-to-dr.md The DR site takes over; later the primary comes back Sync and DR pairings pairings.md Content sync or DR sync between two sites Upgrades and rollbacks upgrades.md A new release put in, and taken back out if needed Moving to a new machine move.md A laptop to a server, or one server to another, nothing lost Security hardening security.md A checklist for a security review A forgotten password or certificate forgotten.md Getting back in Your own database server external-db.md EA Explorer on a PostgreSQL server your DBA manages R6.6.2 Real certificates certificates.md The front door's certificate: your organisation's, uploaded Jenkins jenkins.md A pipeline per eax command and DR tool, a click away R6.6-J1 Database checks db-checks.md Integrity and recent records, weekly and after restores R6.6.1"},{"t":"Backups","u":"install/backups.html","s":"","w":"What is backed up, when, where to keep it, and checking it works. On screen: System Admin Setup Backups, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup backups with --set KEY=VALUE for each value. In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with backups . Your values Value What it is For example --- --- --- <TAG A word to name the backup may be left out before-upgrade <PACK The folder for the DR pack D:/dr-packs Steps 1. A backup now Every database, the files, the config file; <TAG names it. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax backup <TAG Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh backup <TAG 2. The list Newest first, with its size and whether it was checked. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax backups Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh backups 3. Check one restores A trial restore into scratch copies: nothing live touched. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax verify Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh verify 4. Off this machine A DR pack in <PACK , to keep elsewhere guide: DR site . Windows PowerShell : .\\eax dr-pack <PACK Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh dr-pack <PACK 5. The backup and restore test Made, backed up, removed, restored, compared. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax test backup-restore Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh test backup-restore"},{"t":"A catastrophic failure","u":"install/catastrophe.html","s":"","w":"The machine or its data is lost: what to do first, who to tell, what to check. On screen: System Admin Setup A catastrophic failure, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup catastrophe . In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with catastrophe . Steps 1. Stop and look What is lost: the machine, the disk, the data, or only EA Explorer. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax status Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh status 2. Tell people The banner System Admin Banner and the people who rely on it. 3. The newest good backup On this machine, the share, or a DR pack kept elsewhere. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax backups Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh backups 4. A DR site? If there is one, switch to it guide: switch to DR . 5. Otherwise rebuild On a new machine from the backup guide: rebuild ."},{"t":"Real certificates","u":"install/certificates.html","s":"","w":"The front door's certificate: your organisation's, uploaded. On screen: System Admin Setup Real certificates, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup certificates with --set KEY=VALUE for each value. In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with certificates . Your values Value What it is For example --- --- --- <HOSTNAME The name people open EA Explorer at ea.example.org <CERT FILE The certificate file PEM C:/certs/ea.crt <KEY FILE Its private key file PEM, no password C:/certs/ea.key <CHAIN FILE The chain file the issuers' certificates may be left out C:/certs/chain.crt Steps 1. Ask for one Covering <HOSTNAME , reports. <HOSTNAME and docs. <HOSTNAME ; with its private key no password and the chain. 2. Put it in From files on this machine or upload it on System Admin Secrets Front door certificate : checked, used at once, no restart, the one before kept. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax certs front install --cert <CERT FILE --key <KEY FILE --chain <CHAIN FILE Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh certs front install --cert <CERT FILE --key <KEY FILE --chain <CHAIN FILE 3. Check it The names it covers, who issued it, when it ends; undo puts the one before back. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax certs front Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh certs front 4. Expiry Alerts 30 days before and on the day. 5. Laptops trust your authority Company laptops trust your organisation's authority already, or IT adds it."},{"t":"Database checks","u":"install/db-checks.html","s":"","w":"Integrity and recent records, weekly and after restores R6.6.1 . On screen: System Admin Setup Database checks, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup db-checks . In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with db-checks . Steps 1. Check now Every database: indexes, tables, constraints, sequences, the newest records. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax db integrity Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh db integrity 2. Safe fixes Made by themselves after a backup; the admins are told. 3. Orphan rows Database maintenance Integrity Preview the repair Super Admins ."},{"t":"A DR site","u":"install/dr-site.html","s":"","w":"A second site kept up to date, ready to take over. On screen: System Admin Setup A DR site, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup dr-site . In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with dr-site . Steps 1. The DR site A server the server guide with the same release. 2. A pairing key on the DR site System Admin Site pairings Make a key. 3. Pair from the primary System Admin Site pairings Pair with a site: DR sync. 4. Accept on the DR site It becomes read only, kept up to date every few minutes. 5. Rehearse The restore drill, now and then."},{"t":"Your own database server","u":"install/external-db.html","s":"","w":"EA Explorer on a PostgreSQL server your DBA manages R6.6.2 . On screen: System Admin Setup Your own database server, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup external-db with --set KEY=VALUE for each value. In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with external-db . Your values Value What it is For example --- --- --- <DB HOST Your database server's name db.example.org <DB PORT Its port 5432 Steps 1. Your DBA prepares the server deploy/external-db/prepare.sql: the databases, the logins, their rights. 2. Point EA Explorer at it <DB HOST , port <DB PORT : tested before it is saved. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax setup external-db --host <DB HOST --port <DB PORT Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh setup external-db --host <DB HOST --port <DB PORT 3. Start The db container passes connections through; nothing else changes. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax restart Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh restart 4. Backups still run EA Explorer's own backups, over the network; your DBA's on top. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax backup Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh backup"},{"t":"A forgotten password or certificate","u":"install/forgotten.html","s":"","w":"Getting back in. On screen: System Admin Setup A forgotten password or certificate, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup forgotten with --set KEY=VALUE for each value. In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with forgotten . Your values Value What it is For example --- --- --- <USER The administrator's user name eaadmin Steps 1. A person's password Keycloak's Forgot password, or a Keycloak Admin sets one. 2. An administrator locked out <USER gets a temporary password, shown once changed at the next sign-in . Windows PowerShell : .\\eax access reset-password <USER Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh access reset-password <USER 3. Keycloak is down The break-glass account EAX BREAK GLASS PASSWORD . 4. A service's password eax secrets rotate <KEY sets a new one everywhere it is used. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax secrets show Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh secrets show 5. A certificate eax certs renew --force makes them all again. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax certs renew --force Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh certs renew --force 6. Everything else On the machine, the database answers without a network login: eax psql."},{"t":"Jenkins","u":"install/jenkins.html","s":"","w":"A pipeline per eax command and DR tool, a click away R6.6-J1 . On screen: System Admin Setup Jenkins, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup jenkins . In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with jenkins . Steps 1. Start it Its own stack, the agent on this machine, the pipelines written. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax jenkins up Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh jenkins up 2. Sign in With EA Explorer Super or IT Admin , or Jenkins' own account when Keycloak is down. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax jenkins status Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh jenkins status 3. Run a pipeline eax a command Build with parameters; those that change everything ask for the installation's name."},{"t":"A laptop","u":"install/laptop.html","s":"","w":"EA Explorer on your own computer, to try it or to work alone. On screen: System Admin Setup A laptop, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup laptop . In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with laptop . Steps 1. Docker runs Docker Desktop installed and started; at least 16 GB of memory. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax check Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh check 2. The config file Answers laptop and password or certificate . Windows PowerShell : .\\eax init laptop --password Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh init laptop --password 3. Start The core first a few minutes , the rest in the background. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax up Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh up 4. Trust the certificate The browser stops warning about the laptop's own certificate. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax trust Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh trust 5. Check it The smoke test: every role signs in, every area answers. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax test smoke Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh test smoke 6. Sign in https://localhost: the logins are printed by eax logins. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax logins Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh logins"},{"t":"Moving to a new machine","u":"install/move.html","s":"","w":"A laptop to a server, or one server to another, nothing lost. On screen: System Admin Setup Moving to a new machine, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup move with --set KEY=VALUE for each value. In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with move . Your values Value What it is For example --- --- --- <PACK The folder for the DR pack D:/dr-packs <INSTALL The folder EA Explorer is put in on the new machine C:/EA-Explorer Steps 1. A DR pack on the old machine Everything in one folder <PACK , checked; copy it to the new machine. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax dr-pack <PACK Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh dr-pack <PACK 2. The new machine The new machine guide. 3. Build from the pack On the new machine, from <PACK into <INSTALL . Windows PowerShell : .\\dr\\eax-dr.ps1 -Pack <PACK -Install <INSTALL Linux or macOS: ./dr/eax-dr.sh --pack <PACK --install <INSTALL 4. Point people at it The address moved; the old machine stopped."},{"t":"A new machine","u":"install/new-machine.html","s":"","w":"A machine made ready for EA Explorer: Docker, disk, folders, network. On screen: System Admin Setup A new machine, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup new-machine . In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with new-machine . Steps 1. Docker Docker installed; at least 16 GB of memory and 100 GB of disk for a server. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax check Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh check 2. Folders Where data, backups and logs live EAX DATA DIR, EAX BACKUP DIR, EAX LOGS DIR . Windows PowerShell : .\\eax folders Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh folders 3. Network Port 443 open to people; nothing else needs to be. 4. Then The laptop or server guide."},{"t":"Sync and DR pairings","u":"install/pairings.html","s":"","w":"Content sync or DR sync between two sites. On screen: System Admin Setup Sync and DR pairings, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup pairings . In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with pairings . Steps 1. A key on the receiving site System Admin Site pairings Make a key: shown once. 2. Pair from the sending site Its address, the key, content or DR; by hand or by itself. 3. Accept On the receiving site: commit by hand look first or by itself. 4. Sync now On the sending site; the batches show what arrived and what was committed."},{"t":"Building an environment from a backup","u":"install/rebuild.html","s":"","w":"A new machine made from a backup or a DR pack, nothing lost. On screen: System Admin Setup Building an environment from a backup, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup rebuild with --set KEY=VALUE for each value. In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with rebuild . Your values Value What it is For example --- --- --- <PACK The folder for the DR pack D:/dr-packs <INSTALL The folder EA Explorer is put in on the new machine C:/EA-Explorer Steps 1. The pack A DR pack eax dr-pack or a backup folder, with its env file. 2. Docker on the new machine The new machine guide. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax check Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh check 3. Build and restore On the new machine, from the pack in <PACK into <INSTALL : the code, the config, the restore, compared. Windows PowerShell : .\\dr\\eax-dr.ps1 -Pack <PACK -Install <INSTALL Linux or macOS: ./dr/eax-dr.sh --pack <PACK --install <INSTALL 4. Check it The integrity check and the key items. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax db integrity Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh db integrity"},{"t":"Any server over SSH","u":"install/remote.html","s":"","w":"EA Explorer put on another machine from this one no cloud-specific code, D746 . On screen: System Admin Setup Any server over SSH, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup remote . In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with remote . Steps 1. The plan Which machine, how to reach it, laptop or server: the wizard asks. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax deploy --console --plan Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh deploy --console --plan 2. Deploy The code, the config file and the start, over SSH. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax deploy --console --yes Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh deploy --console --yes 3. It appears in the site picker Sites the new site, green within five minutes."},{"t":"Restores","u":"install/restores.html","s":"","w":"A model, a project, a part or everything put back. On screen: System Admin Setup Restores, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup restores with --set KEY=VALUE for each value. In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with restores . Your values Value What it is For example --- --- --- <BACKUP A backup's name, or latest latest Steps 1. A model Model Admin the model Backups Restore over itself or as a new model . 2. A project The project's About tab Back up and restore. 3. A part Backups a backup Restore the databases, the files or the config <BACKUP : a backup's name, or latest . Windows PowerShell : .\\eax restore <BACKUP --what db Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh restore <BACKUP --what db 4. Everything Backups a backup Restore everything: EA Explorer is read only meanwhile. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax restore <BACKUP --what full Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh restore <BACKUP --what full 5. Check it The integrity check runs by itself after every restore guide: database checks . Windows PowerShell : .\\eax db integrity Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh db integrity"},{"t":"Security hardening","u":"install/security.html","s":"","w":"A checklist for a security review. On screen: System Admin Setup Security hardening, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup security with --set KEY=VALUE for each value. In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with security . Your values Value What it is For example --- --- --- <ADDRESS An address or range to let in 10.20.0.0/16 Steps 1. Certificate mode The services sign in with certificates. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax certs Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh certs 2. Multi-factor sign-in System Admin Security: admins or everyone. 3. IP allow-listing System Admin Security Allowed addresses, or from the machine: <ADDRESS let in to the site. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax allow add site <ADDRESS Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh allow add site <ADDRESS 4. Secrets Every password's age; rotation every 90 days. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax secrets show Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh secrets show 5. The front door's certificate The organisation's own guide: certificates . 6. The security test Scans and attacks. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax test security Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh test security"},{"t":"A server","u":"install/server.html","s":"","w":"EA Explorer for a team, on a Linux server with Docker. On screen: System Admin Setup A server, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup server with --set KEY=VALUE for each value. In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with server . Your values Value What it is For example --- --- --- <HOSTNAME The name people open EA Explorer at ea.example.org <CERT FILE The certificate file PEM C:/certs/ea.crt <KEY FILE Its private key file PEM, no password C:/certs/ea.key Steps 1. Docker runs Docker Engine and the compose plugin on the server. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax check Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh check 2. The config file Server mode: strong passwords made; certificates chosen by default; the name people open <HOSTNAME , with DNS records for it, reports. <HOSTNAME and docs. <HOSTNAME . Windows PowerShell : .\\eax init server --certificate --hostname <HOSTNAME Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh init server --certificate --hostname <HOSTNAME 3. The organisation's certificate Covering <HOSTNAME , reports. <HOSTNAME and docs. <HOSTNAME , from files on this machine: checked, then used at once or upload it on System Admin Secrets after the start; guide: certificates . Windows PowerShell : .\\eax certs front install --cert <CERT FILE --key <KEY FILE Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh certs front install --cert <CERT FILE --key <KEY FILE 4. Start The core, then the rest. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax up --wait-all Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh up --wait-all 5. Backups The nightly backup and where it goes guide: backups . Windows PowerShell : .\\eax backups Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh backups 6. Check it The full test, once. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax test full Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh test full"},{"t":"Switching to DR and back","u":"install/switch-to-dr.html","s":"","w":"The DR site takes over; later the primary comes back. On screen: System Admin Setup Switching to DR and back, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup switch-to-dr . In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with switch-to-dr . Steps 1. Take over On the DR site: System Admin Site pairings the DR pairing Stop and take over. 2. Point people at it The address people open DNS moved to the DR site. 3. Check it The integrity check runs by itself when it takes over. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax db integrity Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh db integrity 4. Fail back Pair the other way the DR site sends , then switch back the same way."},{"t":"Upgrades and rollbacks","u":"install/upgrades.html","s":"","w":"A new release put in, and taken back out if needed. On screen: System Admin Setup Upgrades and rollbacks, where you fill in your values and get every command ready to copy. On the machine: eax setup upgrades . In Jenkins: the setup pipeline with upgrades . Steps 1. What is new The releases and their notes. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax update --list Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh update --list 2. A backup first Taken by the update itself too. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax backup Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh backup 3. Update To the newest release of your channel, or a named one. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax update Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh update 4. Check it The smoke test. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax test smoke Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh test smoke 5. Roll back if needed The release before, with its data as it was. Windows PowerShell : .\\eax rollback Linux or macOS: ./eax.sh rollback"},{"t":"EA Explorer 6.7.0: Release 6, secrets and certificates, sync, setup and settings","u":"releases/6.7.0.html","s":"","w":"Release 6 built 17 and 18 Nov 2026; approved and closed 18 Nov 2026 , the owner: \"ok release 6 work is approved\", \"lets close entire 6x line\" : no password in clear text inside the containers, certificates or passwords chosen at the start and rotated when you choose, two sites paired for content or DR, every set-up written down with your own values in the commands, your own certificate on the front door, Jenkins pipelines for every command, and the settings exported and imported . Before updating: take a backup .\\eax backup before-6.7.0 . From 5.7.0 the update runs migrations 0104 to 0107 site pairings and the sync queue: three tables; the integrity checks; the settings' safety copies: one table; the version . Then .\\eax up it rebuilds what changed and keeps your data and .\\eax test smoke . Key and certificate rotation stay off until you switch them on System Admin › Secrets, or the first-run step Upkeep . Secrets and certificates Release 6.0, D743 to D746, D751 - Every password and key is a file under /run/secrets in its own container, never an environment variable: docker inspect , process lists and logs show none. The config file keeps only where they are. - Certificate mode or password mode , chosen at eax init --certificate or --password : in certificate mode EA Explorer runs its own small certificate authority and each service signs in to the database with its own certificate; eax certs switch moves an installation over later. - System Admin › Secrets : every password, key and certificate by name never its value , its age, its next rotation; rotate one, or Rotate all behind the maintenance page asked first , now, at a time, or monthly or every three months. From the machine: eax secrets rotate , eax secrets rotate --all --restart . - The SQL window needs no database password in certificate mode: your EA Explorer sign-in decides. - Restores and DR reset the logins , so a backup from any date restores after the passwords have rotated. - OpenBao and the cloud-specific deploy kinds are removed: no platform-specific code D746 . Site pairings and sync Release 6.5, D749, D753 - System Admin › Site pairings : pair two EA Explorer sites one way, for content sync models, projects, the organisation's content or DR sync everything, the DR site kept read only and up to date ; batches in order, each answered, committed by hand or by themselves; Stop and take over on the DR site. - Content promotion through git : a model's package, a project's backup or a settings file put on any git repository over HTTPS, and taken back from it on another site. - The site's purpose PROD, PRE-PROD, UAT, TEST, DEV, CONTENT, DR, TRAINING shown at the top of every screen: a label only. Setup, guided and documented Release 6.6, D750, D757 to D772 - System Admin › Setup : nineteen guides as documents a laptop, a server, any server over SSH, a new machine, backups, restores, a catastrophic failure, rebuilding from a backup, a DR site, switching to DR, pairings, upgrades, moving machines, security, a forgotten password, your own database server, certificates, Jenkins, database checks . Give your values the server's name, the certificate and key files, the pack folder... and every command is filled in , for Windows or Linux and macOS, to copy, or the whole guide downloaded. Nothing runs from the page. The same guides: eax setup <guide --set KEY=VALUE , and the files in docs/guides . - Database integrity checks , weekly and after every restore: indexes, tables, constraints, sequences, the newest records; safe fixes only when you switch them on; anything that touches rows waits for a Super Admin. - Your own database server : eax setup external-db --host <server , tested before it is saved; EA Explorer's own backups still run over the network. - Your organisation's certificate on the front door: uploaded on System Admin › Secrets or put in from files eax certs front install --cert <file --key <file , checked, used at once with no restart, the one before kept. - The name people open eax hostname set <name , or eax init --hostname . - Jenkins eax jenkins up : a pipeline for every eax command and DR tool, and admin tasks by group start and stop, getting back in, certificates, backup and DR, settings, upkeep ; those that change everything need the installation's name. Runs in Jenkins' sandbox, opening no window on Windows. Tested end to end in Release 7 R7.8 . - Getting an administrator back in from the machine: eax access reset-password unlock mfa-off <user . - Anything that puts the maintenance page up asks first on the screens; eax restart takes down a maintenance page left behind. Settings exported and imported Release 6.7, D755, D768 - System Admin › Settings › Settings import and export Super Admins : one file, the parts you tick application, system and security settings, branding, alerts, keep-for rules, report audiences, webhooks, pairings' settings, the banner, the IP allow lists, the schedules . Never content, people, a password, key or certificate. - Import shows every difference first here and in the file ; you tick what to take; a safety copy is kept first and Undo puts it back; nothing here is ever removed. A file from a newer release is refused. - The same from the machine eax settings export import copies undo , from Jenkins, and through git. Fixed - The restore drill takes the backup straight out of EA Explorer, signs in to the DR copy to decide, and leaves the DR copy running for you to look at. - Rotate all no longer leaves a service half made again; on Windows what makes services again runs from PowerShell only. - Check the integrity now no longer puts the maintenance page up. - The self-test's runner gets the database passwords they are files now ; a stopped test runner is not an alert. - The UI review eax test ui-review is removed."},{"t":"EA Explorer 5.7.0: Release 5.7, branding, customer journeys and the deck tools","u":"releases/5.7.0.html","s":"","w":"Release 5.7 built 17 Nov 2026; the owner: \"build 5.7\"; accepted 17 Nov 2026 : the views' ArchiMate icons first a bug , then logo and branding , customer journey maps , a presentation deck with your own AI through MCP, and the backup and restore test on all of it . Before updating: take a backup .\\eax backup before-5.7.0 . From 5.6.0 the update runs migrations 0100 to 0103 branding: two tables; customer journeys: seven tables; the version; fonts for the themes: one table . A clean rebuild is needed: the API it gains the Pillow library, version 13 , the screens, the sample data and the backup test change .\\eax clean-restart . Then .\\eax test full , which ends with the backup and restore test, and the DR drill .\\dr\\eax-drill . Logo and branding R5.7-B1, D729 - System admin › Branding Super Admins : upload the organisation's logo shown in the top bar and a small icon for the browser tab , and give the name in the top bar EA Explorer then shows small beside it . - Sixteen themes ship : Standard light, today's look , Dark, High contrast for accessibility , Corporate muted , and twelve colours: Blue, Red, Green, Teal, Purple, Orange, Rose, Indigo, Gold, Graphite, Navy and Sand. Choosing a theme shows it at once on your screen so you see how it feels; Save makes it permanent. Choose the organisation's theme, and switch on whether each person may pick their own on My profile › My look. - A theme designer : start from a copy of any theme and change its colours with colour pickers, its fonts the computers' own , text size and corners; every change shows at once, and Save keeps it as a theme of your own. - Your own fonts : upload a WOFF2, WOFF, TrueType or OpenType file under a family name with its bold and italic files if you have them ; the theme designer offers it, and every screen loads it from EA Explorer itself. - Your own themes as CSS : download any theme as a CSS file, change its colours, fonts and corners, and add it back under a name; replace or remove the ones you added. A theme may hold only looks: anything that loads from elsewhere or runs is refused, with the line it is on. - Nobody is locked out : Standard look in each person's menu puts the standard look on in that browser, and a break-glass session always has it. - Only EA Explorer's own screens change: the sign-in page, Reports, Documents, draw.io and the files EA Explorer makes keep their own look. Branding is in the database, so backups, restores and site copies carry it. - Sample data: a theme, Meridian teal sample , added and not chosen. - Migration 0100 two tables . Customer journey maps R5.7-J1, D730 - A project's Customer journeys tab, beside the Business model canvas: any number of journeys, each a grid of stages across and, under each stage, its steps, touchpoints, pain points, moments that matter and opportunities ; personas for the whole journey; a cell edited by clicking it. - How the person feels : each step's emotion from -2 to +2 with faces , drawn as a curve above the steps. - Your own kinds of part and fields for example Systems behind it with an Owner , and extra fields on the standard kinds. - Linked to the models : a stage or a part links to elements of the project's models capabilities, value streams, business services, applications, data, actors and roles . - Versions like the canvas : current state, target state, working copy, scenario; draft or agreed; make a copy the target from today , compare two stage by stage added, changed with the old text and face, removed ; copy to another project; every change kept. - Export a journey or a comparison as PDF, PowerPoint or draw.io the drawn view for presentations . - MCP tools customer journey and change customer journey , so your own AI can draft a journey from interviews. - Start blank or from the starter template six typical stages . Sample data: Make a motor claim today and in 2028 in Protea Claims Transformation 2028, and Buy pet insurance from the starter in Fynbos Pet Insurance launch. - Project backups carry journeys. Migration 0101 seven tables . Documentation › Customer journeys. A presentation deck with your own AI R5.7-P1, D731 - Three MCP tools so your own AI builds a deck about a project in your own client, in its own look; nothing is saved back to EA Explorer: - deck outline : a suggested outline from where the project is the phase now, what is done, what is open ; - deck sources : everything a deck may draw on the project, phases, deliverables and their documents, models, views, drawn views, decisions, risks, issues, requirements, key questions, sign-offs, stakeholders, canvases and journeys , each with its source, so a slide can say where it came from; - view picture : a view or drawn view as a PNG or an SVG , drawn as on the screens with the ArchiMate icons, or as its raw data to draw your own. - Only what you may read; a document marked NOT FOR AI USE OR AUTOMATED PROCESSING by its title only. - The API gains the Pillow library for the PNG . Documentation › A presentation deck with your own AI. The backup and restore test covers 5.7 R5.7-T1 - eax test backup-restore and the DR drill, which runs it now also makes a customer journey from the starter, a step with its emotion, a persona, a pain point, a part of a kind added by people with its field, a link to a model element, a target-state copy and a comparison , an uploaded theme and the test account's own theme , and calls the deck tools . Each is read back, gone after restoring B1 and back exactly after B2; after the restores the deck tools read the restored project and the journey still compares with its target. - The test never changes what everyone sees: the organisation's logo and theme are left alone, and what it made is removed at the end. The demo project D734 - Sign in as demo-super-admin a new laptop account, a Super Admin; the sample password : Protea Claims Transformation 2028 sample and its models are pinned, and the project now holds every kind of content in one place: canvases, jour"},{"t":"EA Explorer 5.6.0: Release 5.6, backup and restore tested","u":"releases/5.6.0.html","s":"","w":"Release 5.6 built 16 and 17 Nov 2026; the owner: \"Build 5.6\"; accepted 17 Nov 2026 : the backup and restore test the owner set out, job priorities , updates and deployments from the published GitHub Releases only , disaster recovery the DR pack, the DR tool and the automated restore drill , and the drills as documents with a PDF. Before updating: take a backup .\\eax backup before-5.6.0 . From 5.5.0 the update runs migrations 0098 and 0099 job priorities: two tables; the version . A clean rebuild is needed: the API, the job runner, the operations helper, the backup container, the screens and the eax command change .\\eax clean-restart . Then .\\eax test full , which now ends with the backup and restore test it asks nothing . The backup and restore test R5.6-B1 The owner's test: \"do an infra backup ... B1; create a project with some models; create content ... documents, custom reports and custom views in various states, tags and all other kind of content; do an infra backup B2; restore B1: the projects and models should be gone; restore B2: all content should now be checked including files using checksum\". - .\\eax test backup-restore also .\\eax test restore , and last in .\\eax test full : a test style of its own, synchronous . eax runs one command after another and waits for each: the backups and restores in the operations helper, the content through the REST API and MCP in the API container. No test container, no background task, no job queue. Each step is printed with its result; the first step that fails stops the test and says which and why. - On this installation, asking nothing : it says first, plainly, that anything done meanwhile is lost. Then the maintenance page goes on for everyone and everything in the background stops every recurring job, the scheduled backups, commands and updates; what misses a turn runs at its next one ; both come back when it ends, whatever happened. Jobs the test itself needs a project's folders in Documents still run. - B1 a random name , then content of every kind : a project and its models entities, relationships, a drawn view, a child model with its own change, an uncommitted change, a tag , a KPI, a custom view, project steps, a key question, a stakeholder and a discussion, a Business Model Canvas, a document class with a document and its file, an ADR linked to an element, a dispensation, a discovery project with a source and a whole run Found in, a skipped item , two test accounts with their roles, and a file in persist/ and in the import folder. - B2 a random name . B1 restored : everything made is gone, and every table of every database and every file of every file set is as at B1. B1 restored again : the same fingerprint S8 . B2 restored : everything is back row for row, and every database's rows and every file's checksum are as at B2 the documents, the certificate, the reports' home, the import and export folders, persist/ and the config file . - After B2 : the test's accounts sign in S1 ; search finds the restored elements and the KPI is read S4 ; a new element, a commit, a tag, a document and a new ADR numbered after the last all work S5 ; no job ran twice and none is left running S6 ; the document downloads with the checksum it was uploaded with S7 . - Refused before anything is touched when the disk is short, saying how much is needed S12 . The scheduled clean-up never removes B1, B2 or a pinned backup S14 . No password, key or token in the report or the restores' logs S13 . The times of each backup and restore, the recovery time and the recovery point are in the report S15 . - When it fails after B1 was restored , B2 is restored first, so the installation is as it was; the backups are kept and named. When it passes , the test's data and both backups and the backups the restores took first are removed. - The report : work/tests/backup-restore-<time /report.md and report.json, and Self-test › History. - It replaces the old restore suite R3.8 : a self-test run no longer restores anything. The restore drills R5.6-B1 Two documents in Documentation › Administration and operations , numbered command-line steps with what to check after each, each with Download PDF : Restore drill: EA Explorer onto a new machine and Restore drill: once a month . Disaster recovery: eax-dr and eax-drill R5.6-B2 A dr folder that runs on its own, copied anywhere outside an installation PowerShell and bash forms; nothing asked : - eax-dr builds a whole environment from an infrastructure backup: give it the backup's folder, the folder to install into, a copy of the env file and the code a DR pack's, a copy eax drill code made, or a published release from GitHub . It checks the backup and the code file by file against their checksums, copies the code in no GitHub needed , puts the env file and the backup in place, builds and starts EA Explorer, restores everything with the maintenance page on, starts it again and runs the smoke test. - eax-drill is the restore drill, automated: give it a running installation, a new folder for the DR copy and a temp folder. It checks the installation runs, makes test content, takes a full backup, shuts the installation down containers removed; its data and images kept , copies the backup, the env file and its own code into the temp folder, builds the DR copy with eax-dr from that code no GitHub in the new folder under its own Docker name its own volumes and restores it, then compares every table and file and the test content with before and runs the smoke test. The installation's folder and data are never touched; the DR copy is left running, and the report gives the recovery time and how to go back. - eax dr-pack <folder makes a DR pack in one command on the running installation: the maintenance page on for a few minutes, a fingerprint of every table and file, a full backup, then the pack: the backup, VERSION.txt , the env file, the code as it runs code/ , so changes and customisations made on the machine come too and the new machine needs n"},{"t":"EA Explorer 5.5.0: Release 5.5, enterprise discovery","u":"releases/5.5.0.html","s":"","w":"Release 5.5 16 Nov 2026; the owner: \"Build this release\" : enterprise discovery , run by the people's own AI through MCP; architecture decision records and dispensations in the Governance Log; and the Live browser full screen . Before updating: take a backup .\\eax backup before-5.5.0 . From 5.1.0 the update runs migrations 0093 to 0097 decision records and dispensations, enterprise discovery, the version, the MCP suite, two indexes: tables, columns, two roles, rows, constraints and indexes . A clean rebuild is needed: the API, the MCP server, the job runner, Keycloak's realm two new roles and the screens change .\\eax clean-restart . Then .\\eax test full . Enterprise discovery R5.5 The owner's design leads: \"EA explorer will only be source and sink of information. Let MCP and LLm run this one\". EA Explorer keeps the setup and takes back what is found; it never signs in to a source at run time, never reads or transcribes anything, holds no AI key and runs nothing on a timer. - Discovery projects AI MCP › Enterprise discovery : a name, the target model the AI commits into a child of the main model to review first, or the main model once you trust the AI , the defaults of a run, and a schedule. - A new global role, Discovery Admin eax-discovery-admin : sets up discovery projects and their sources for any model; Super Admins can too. Everyone who may read a project's target model sees it and its runs. - Sources of every kind : mailboxes, document folders and shares, FTP, SFTP, SharePoint, Git repositories, wikis, ticket systems and the CMDB, Teams and Slack channels, database schemas read only , cloud storage, cloud accounts and recordings. Each says where it is, what to include and whether attachments are read. - Test, then forget : a Discovery Admin types a source's sign-in a key or token, a user name and password, a client certificate, or single sign-on to Test the link ; it is used once and forgotten. Only the method and the result are kept. At run time the AI brings its own access. - The AI runs it through MCP with its own sign-in: run discovery project <name asks whether to read only what is new or everything, and whether to mark or delete what is gone the project's defaults suggested . The target model is tagged before and after every run, so comparing the two tags shows what the run changed, the metamodel first. - Found in : every element and relationship the AI adds or changes keeps where it was found the source, the item, where in it, a link . An element's new Found in tab shows it. - \"AI agent on behalf of\" the person who set the project up: the run's commit, its tags and its Found in say so. - May be the same as : where the AI is unsure an element is new, it adds it and flags the one it may duplicate; merge them with Dedupe, then mark the flag Dealt with. - NOT FOR AI USE OR AUTOMATED PROCESSING is respected: such items are never read; their title, place and date are listed in the run's report as skipped. - Decision records and dispensations found in the sources are logged by the AI as Drafts in the organisation's Governance Log, with where they were found; the Architecture Board accepts or rejects them. - The schedule is a marker : the AI client's own scheduled task asks discovery projects due and runs each. A run more than two hours late shows as Overdue on the project and raises an alert System Admin › Alerts . - Eight MCP tools: discovery projects , discovery projects due , run discovery project , discovery record found , discovery report skipped , discovery log decision , discovery finish run , discovery run report . - The sample data adds a discovery project on the demo estate with five sources example addresses; no sign-in kept . Architecture decision records and dispensations R5.5.1 - ADRs and dispensations, first-class : numbered per year across the organisation ADR-2026-001, DISP-2026-001 , each with its template an ADR's context, options, decision, rationale and consequences; a dispensation's waived standard, systems, justification, risks and remediation , its ADM phase, record type or sponsor, and a lifecycle. - The organisation's own Governance Log Repository › Governance Log : the new Architecture Board role eax-architecture-board logs, accepts and rejects records outside any project; in a project, its sign-off people do. - Links both ways : to elements, requirements, principles, standards and other records; a newer ADR that supersedes an older one marks it Superseded. An element's Linked decisions and dispensations tab shows them. - Dispensations end : every dispensation has an expiry date; its owner, sponsor and the Board are told before it ends 30 days, a setting and on the day, when it becomes Expired. - The governance report : decisions by status and project, active dispensations by expiry date, on screen and as an OData feed for BI tools /api/v1/odata/governance/ . Self-test - An MCP suite .\\eax test mcp ; Self-test › MCP; part of the full test : the MCP server called over HTTP exactly as an AI client calls it, no language model. Every tool listed; every tool that reads called with the run's own data and never a server error; a change kept as the person's own; refused without a token, with a read-only token and without the role; every call in the AI activity log R5.5.5 . - Enterprise discovery and decision records in the API suite : a discovery project, its sources and Test the link through REST, then a whole run through MCP as an AI makes it the reading assumed , and the decision records and dispensations through REST, 28 checks R5.5.4 . - The Live browser full screen R5.5.2 : Self-test › Watch › Full screen fills the screen with the test's browser; a thin bar shows the step with Pause, Continue and Step, and hides after three seconds Esc leaves . - The page sweep opens the Governance Log and Enterprise discovery. Also in this release - Template setup › Templates: View and Download for every template that has its file. View shows it here without downloading: a"},{"t":"EA Explorer 5.1.0: Release 5.1, stabilisation","u":"releases/5.1.0.html","s":"","w":"Release 5.1, a stabilisation release 16 Nov 2026; the owner: \"release this as a stabalization release before we do any more work\"; \"make it 5.1\" : the bugs found running 5.0.0 on a laptop and in its full self-test, fixed, each with a test that fails without its fix D599 ; the job queue made visible and safe to look after; nothing new beyond that. Before updating: take a backup .\\eax backup before-5.1.0 . From 5.0.0 the update runs migrations 0090 to 0092 the self-test's Jobs suite, two indexes for the service desk, the version; constraints, indexes and a row only . A clean rebuild is needed: the API's start-up, the job runner, the screens and the test runner change .\\eax clean-restart . Then .\\eax test full . The job queue - A database connection was ended every five minutes : the idle-session clean-up ended every connection on the server, not only idle ones. This was behind sample data stuck part-way, projects missing and backups that hung R5.36 . - System Admin › Running › Jobs : what is being worked on and what waits, in words; Kill, Cancel, Move up and down; the stuck ones counted on the dashboard with what to do, and an alert. Nothing is killed without a person saying so R5.30 . The same from the command line: eax jobs R5.35 . - Job slots set on screen , on Scaling and Containers, with a warning past the machine's CPU threads R5.33 ; the job history deleted on screen R5.34 . - Each scheduled job runs one copy at a time R5.30, R5.32 ; the industry packs load for at most 8 minutes a run and carry on at the next R5.32 , and their lock is never ended by database maintenance R5.38 . - Jobs left by a job runner that stopped are marked stopped when it starts again, so they no longer show as being worked on and their next runs start; each of the three job runners is watched R5.45, R5.46 . - Kill, Cancel, Move and Delete history work they failed on the job runner's own database rules ; Kill asks a running job to stop, and a second Kill marks one no runner has any more as stopped R5.45, R5.46 . - Waiting jobs say why : behind the earlier run of the same job, or put off to a later time, instead of \"stuck\" R5.46 . - The library models move once : the start-up step and the scheduled job no longer move them at the same time R5.43 . Screens - A service request shows the project and the model by name, not by identifier R5.37 . - Operations and Personal data no longer flicker to \"starting\" when the API is busy R5.39 . - A value a caller gets wrong not an identifier, not a date, not JSON is answered \"not valid\" 400 , never a server error R5.40 . - System Admin › Logs: the containers in a drop-down with a tick each, the time window labelled, and step-by-step help R5.42 . - The versions on the start-up status : the API, its database and the code on this machine; down when the API and the database differ, a warning when the code is newer than what runs rebuild before testing ; the self-test checks the running version and says when its runner was built from other code R5.48 . - System Admin › SQL: names only in the tree, with a Properties panel for the database, schema, table or view chosen R5.44 . Testing - A Jobs suite in the self-test and the full test eax test jobs : the job runner takes jobs, the alert checks run, nothing stuck, every scheduled job has its lock, Cancel, Move and Kill work on probe jobs rolled back R5.46 . - Each area's passed and failed on the self-test's area cards, while a run goes on and for a finished run R5.47 . - How many checks have run and are left in each phase , big on screen R5.5.3 . - The full test no longer backs up and restores the infrastructure eax test backup-restore does , and never runs the performance test R5.29, R5.31 . - Fixed in the tests themselves EA Explorer was not failing : the Reports suite read only the first 100 dashboards and counted chart requests aborted by moving to the next dashboard; the cross-model attack used addresses that had changed R5.47 . Installing and starting - .\\eax clean-restart no longer stops when Windows cannot start docker for one look \"The paging file is too small\" : it says so and waits on R5.41 . Not in this release Everything recorded for later stays there: Release 5.5 enterprise discovery, decision records , Release 5.6 pausing a test, job priorities and fair turns, every job reviewed, Updates and Deploy from GitHub Releases , Release 6.6 setup guides, database checks, an external database server, real certificates and Release 5.7 customer journey maps ."},{"t":"EA Explorer 5.0.0: Release 5","u":"releases/5.0.0.html","s":"","w":"Release 5 released 15 Nov 2026; D696: built whole, tested with the automation, its bugs fixed, then released, nothing carried forward : running EA Explorer on a server with confidence: security at the front door, alerts, logs, database maintenance, an optimisation report, a service desk, and testing that runs by itself. Before updating: take a backup .\\eax backup before-5.0.0 . From 4.0.0 the update runs migrations 0078 to 0089 machine credentials' addresses, the Auditor role, alerts, database maintenance runs, the service desk and its rework, the optimisation reports, the performance suite, sizing estimates, the live browser, a duplicate index removed, the version; tables and data only . A clean rebuild is needed: the operations helper, the front door's configuration, the set-up and the test runner change .\\eax clean-restart . Then .\\eax test full . Security - IP allow lists at the front door, per place the screens, sign-in, administration, MCP, machine access , never locking out the person who sets them; a machine credential limited to its own addresses R5.2, D686; eax allow . - Multi-factor sign-in as a setting, off by default: for admins or everyone R5.3, D690 . - The Auditor role eax-audit : sees everything a Super Admin sees, changes nothing, never sees a secret R5.22, D693 . - Signed deployments , for an organisation that wants them: eax sign and eax verify ; an update refuses a version not signed by a trusted key once one is trusted R5.10, D685 . - Automated security testing : weekly by itself and nightly in CI; a signed-in ZAP scan; code, secrets and licence scanning; the attacks of Release 3 kept as tests; a gate on high and critical findings with accepted ones that expire; the trend on Self-test › Security and an alert on a new finding R5.17, D698 . Operations - Alerts : checks with levels, hold, flapping, acknowledge, silence, escalation, email and webhooks R5.9, D689 . - Logs : levels, every container's logs kept and rolled, the web log of every call, on System Admin › Logs R5.6 to R5.8, D688 . - Log files roll at a size set on System Admin › Logs Size and keeping : 100 KB by default for every log file, and for Docker's own copy of each container's output from the next .\\eax up ; kept 7 days, however many files R5.26, D701 . - Database maintenance : every database checked daily, tidied nightly without locks, compacting and lock resolution after a preview R5.12, D691; eax db . - The optimisation report : monthly suggestions with their evidence and the people who made and look after each model or project, applied only with a yes, for a whole model or project; on screen and as Excel R5.1, D697; eax optimise . - Server sizing : a best estimate of RAM, CPU and disk, per container too, with a compose override R5.19; eax estimate . - Where the data lives : one base folder, a folder per kind of data R5.4, D687; eax folders . - The service desk : choose a group, then what you need or \"Something else\" ; every request goes to the Super Admins, who assign it to a person R5.11, R5.27, D692, D700; eax ticket . - The version review every three months, as a scheduled task R5.21, D694 . Testing - Performance testing : eax test performance , k6 with many people at once, compared with the last release's baseline; run only when asked for, never as part of the full test R5.18, D695, R5.29 . - Watch the tests' browsers live , streamed only while watched; slow motion and pause after each step; every journey's video and trace kept for a watched run R5.20; eax test watch --browser . For developers - Every module, class and function documented , kept so by a test; docs/functional-description.md R5.14, R5.15 . - docs/handover.md and eax dev check for whoever takes the work over R5.16 . Fixed while testing - The clean rebuild stopped at the Reports image: it asked for an image library Pillow 13 that Superset 6.1.0 cannot run. Superset's own version is kept; its findings are accepted until the version review on 1 Feb 2027, because the features that use it are off R5.23, D699 . - After the clean rebuild the site could not be reached: one line of the front door's configuration the web log's day was written in a way nginx refuses, so it never started R5.24 . - Multi-factor sign-in turned off still asked for a code from people who had set one up when it was on: turning it off now also removes the codes EA Explorer asked people to set up R5.25 . - Database maintenance found the background tasks' index made twice: the extra one is removed R5.28 ."},{"t":"EA Explorer 4.0.0: Release 4","u":"releases/4.0.0.html","s":"","w":"Release 4 accepted 15 Nov 2026 : Reports on Superset 6.1.0 and tested as people use them, an AI MCP menu of its own with tools to run the installation, project steps in your own order, and the bugs of the last two full tests. Before updating: take a backup .\\eax backup before-4.0.0 . From 3.5.0 the update runs migrations 0075 to 0077 the self-test's reports suite, a step's history may say it was moved, and the version; nothing removed . The reports image is new Superset 6.1.0 : .\\eax update rebuilds it; the report dashboards are imported again at its first start a few minutes . After it, run .\\eax test smoke . Known issue, for Release 5.6: in the full self-test, \"backup: an infrastructure backup\" can end with \"RemoteDisconnected\" after about six minutes the backup itself is checked by the backup and restore suites . Reports - Apache Superset 6.1.0 from 4.1.2 , with every report chart and setting checked against it R4.7, D680 . - Report links open their report : clicking a report from a model lands on that dashboard, signed in once through Keycloak, also when already signed in to Reports. - The report dashboards are imported at every start of Reports its container now sees them , each said in its log. - A self-test suite for Reports eax test reports , and in the full test : Keycloak test users sign in as people do; every dashboard opens with every chart answering, as the Super Admin and the Report Viewer; each person sees only their own models and only committed content; the IT Admin sees none; the files reports make open R4.1, D681 . AI MCP - AI MCP is a menu of its own, for everyone : Connect, What it can do, My AI activity and, for admins, Everyone's AI activity R4.20 . - Tools to run the installation for Super Admins and IT Admins: its state, the resource history, what is slowing things down in words, worst first , container logs, backups and unused models and projects; and, each previewed and then confirmed, take a backup, restore one, change the number of API and job servers, archive a model or a project. Never while the self-test or a restore runs; nothing deleted R4.22, D683 . Projects - The ADM steps in your own order : move a step up or down in its phase ▲▼ , say where a new step goes, and set the order in the project wizard; the step's history says it was moved R4.21 . Command line and documentation - docs/starting.md : the first start and every start after, step by step, on a laptop and a server. - eax 's screen no longer quits to the command prompt after each command R4.11 . Fixed - A body that is not JSON sent to a model's archive was acted on; three server errors where \"not found\" belongs; System Admin › Scaling failed when a container had just gone R4.13 to R4.15 . - The self-test's own mistakes long answers cut, values not quoted, the iteration journey's step 14 R4.16, R4.17 . - The Superset image's critical findings: Pillow 13 and a newer uv R4.24 . - Documents on the Health page says it is answering instead of \"HTTP 302\". Not in this release The key vault OpenBao was built and then switched off by the owner: it is Release 6, discussed before it is brought in. Moved to Release 5: the code documentation and handover R4.3 to R4.5 , automated security and performance testing R4.8, R4.9 , server sizing R4.10 , watching the screen tests live R4.12 , the three-monthly version review R4.23 ; the backup issue above is Release 5.6."},{"t":"EA Explorer 3.5.0: Release 3.5","u":"releases/3.5.0.html","s":"","w":"Release 3.5 14 Nov 2026 : memory. How much each container needs is measured, in one go or all the time, and the laptop needs less: two containers fewer and Documents and Keycloak sized for where they run. Before updating: take a backup .\\eax backup before-3.5.0 . From 3.0.0 the update runs migrations 0073 and 0074 the resource history's table, and the version; nothing removed . The operations and personal containers are gone: .\\eax update and .\\eax clean-restart remove them by hand: docker compose down --remove-orphans . After it, run .\\eax test smoke . Known issues, fixed in Release 4 R4.13 to R4.17, as in 3.0.0 : a body that is not JSON sent to a model's archive is acted on; three server errors where \"not found\" belongs; System Admin › Scaling fails when a container has just gone; the iteration journey's step 14; and some of the self-test's own checks. The resource history - Memory, CPU, disk and the database's cache, recorded all the time : every 15 minutes, while people work and while the self-test runs, each container's memory, CPU, network and disk, the Docker host's memory left and swap, the file systems and the database's cache hit rate, size and connections are kept, each sample marked with what was happening a self-test, a backup, a restore, a start-up R3.5-M8, D679 . - On System Admin › Footprint : charts over 6 hours to 90 days or a period of your own, the busy stretches shaded; each container's average and peak; CSV; the interval off, 1 to 60 minutes and how long it is kept every sample 7 days, then one an hour; 90 days in all ; a shorter interval for a test that goes back by itself. A Super Admin deletes a period, everything before a date or all of it audited . eax footprint --history days on the command line. Measuring memory - eax footprint --watch minutes label : every container's memory every 15 seconds, its lowest, average and peak, the whole installation's peak beside the guide 10 GB on a laptop, EAX MEMORY TARGET MB; a guide, not a limit and whether the Docker host paged. Every self-test run is watched the same way memory.md in its folder . - eax measure : restart if asked , start-up, a snapshot, the smoke test, at rest, in use and the full test, each checked, carried on with --from N , ending in one summary work/footprint/measure- .md . --no-full leaves the full test out; on a server it is safe by default no clean restart, no full test unless asked R3.5-M1 . Less memory on a laptop - One API again : the operations and personal data services are served by the API container D677 : about 0.35 GB. Their data keeps its own schemas and connection strings, and a part can run in a container of its own again by configuration only EAX SERVE and EAX OPERATIONS INTERNAL URL or EAX PERSONAL INTERNAL URL R3.5-M1b . - Documents Mayan : its workers were one process per processor core; now EAX MAYAN WORKER CONCURRENCY laptop 1, server 2 and EAX MAYAN WEB WORKERS laptop 2, server 3 : about 1.5 GB on a laptop. Large OCR jobs take longer. - Keycloak : its Java heap by EAX KEYCLOAK HEAP laptop -Xms64m -Xmx512m, server -Xms256m -Xmx1024m : about 0.2 GB. Fixed - A self-test run was sometimes \"not measured\": its memory watch now finishes before the run ends. - System Admin › Footprint broke and the screen tests after it when eax measure 's progress file was in its folder. - eax measure 's summary, carried on with --from , listed every earlier attempt and called start-up paging a problem."},{"t":"EA Explorer 3.0.0: Release 3","u":"releases/3.0.0.html","s":"","w":"Release 3 14 Nov 2026 : data discovery and ingestion a reverse OData feed, pushes with a Python kit, documents read by AI, all reviewed as deliveries , Import and export guided step by step both ways, and testing that proves the whole product: negative tests for every endpoint, code coverage graphs, watching a run, the restore suite, the API harness, a security review with a Content-Security-Policy, and the eax screen. Before updating: take a backup .\\eax backup before-3.0.0 . From 2.0.0 the update runs migrations 0068 to 0072 the restore suite, the API harness's cases, text indexes, discovery; indexes and tables only, nothing removed . Clean rebuilds now fetch current base images, so the first one takes longer. After it, run .\\eax test full . Known issues, fixed in Release 4 from the last full self-test, R4.13 to R4.17 : a body that is not JSON sent to a model's archive is acted on it archives the model ; three server errors where \"not found\" belongs; System Admin › Scaling fails when a container has just gone; the iteration journey's step 14; and some of the self-test's own checks. Data discovery and ingestion - A reverse OData feed : Import and export › Discovery points a model at an OData feed EA Explorer reads, an endpoint other systems push to, or documents the AI engine reads. EA Explorer discovers the sets, fields and keys, suggests where each goes, and each run now, daily or weekly sends only what is new or changed as a delivery to preview and accept; names close to existing elements are suggested as matches to confirm. The AI engine is off until a Super Admin chooses one: cloud with your own key, or local the Release 3 epic, D670; docs/discovery.md . - Push with Python : a push source's Discovery panel shows a short Python script to copy and downloads it as a kit the script, requirements.txt, a README with the venv steps, sample CSVs from the model's metamodel : it reads CSV files and pushes them with push dataframe url, df, username, password , or a token, API key or client certificate D674 . Its samples are a file for every entity type of the model, each showing a relationship the metamodel allows, and the README lists how each relationship is published. - Import and export, step by step : Bring data in and Take data out guide you from \"where is the data?\" or \"what is it for?\" to the right screen and the review, whichever way the data comes or goes D676 . - Delete a discovery source after a confirm; refused while a delivery of it waits; what it delivered stays, D675 . The eax command - eax screen : a full-screen eax in the style of Turbo Pascal, opened by plain eax : menus with Alt letters and the mouse, a dialog per command that shows the command as you fill it, a live dashboard of the containers and disks, and output in a window or the plain terminal; the numbered eax menu stays R3.1, D669 . Administration - A full file explorer : a container's Files tab has File, Edit and View menus and a right-click menu, Details, List and Large icons views and a Preview pane, keys F2, Delete, Ctrl+C / X / V / A and more , choosing several at once one zip, cut, copy, move, delete , Properties, and drag and drop to upload or move; System Admin › Mounts opens a mount in the same explorer R3.5, D668 . - Users shows projects too : System Admin › Users › People lists each person's projects with their roles beside their models with their roles, as two plain lists; the CSV has a Projects column R3.3 . Estate - Clean estate diagrams : System Admin › Estate draws every line at right angles around the boxes with an arrowhead and a label, keeps text inside its box, lists each host folder once single files and finished one-shot containers apart , and keeps the logical columns level; the draw.io downloads keep the same routes R3.4, D667 . Speed - Faster text searches : exact name lookups go through a hashed-name index, and Find, search and filters through trigram indexes on every column they look in name, display id, description, merged-away names ; migration 0070 R3.7, D665 . Testing - GitHub's checks pass again : the API tests ran into \"No module named 'eax'\" on every push since 5 Nov 2026 R3.15, D657 . - Browser journeys on a busy machine : a step that looks in a row or a pop-up waits for it to appear; saving an iteration and sending a merge request are given longer; a failed step also says what an open dialog showed R3.14, D658 . - The full backup-and-restore test : eax test restore and the end of eax test full from the command line backs the installation up, changes it, restores it every way all models, one model, and the infrastructure backup part by part and checks all the content each time; a safety backup is put back if anything fails R3.8, D659 . - The upgrade test checks the way back : the updater's own backup is checked and eax rollback is run and checked; a runbook for upgrading 1.0.0 to 2.0.0 on a laptop and a server R3.11, D660 . - Far fewer skipped checks : the self-test finds the ids it needs from the lists it can read, checks the heavy reads in a bounded way, mounts persist/ in every runner and opens the break-glass page on its own R3.13, D661 . - API test harness Self-test › API harness, and eax test api : pick any endpoint, call it as yourself or a test role, see the answer and the same call as a curl line; save calls as cases the self-test runs too R3.16, D662 . - Negative tests for every endpoint : the full self-test sends every write bad JSON and a list where an object belongs, every read an id that is not there, and long names inside its test data; a server error or a success fails the check. Code coverage under 90% is a warning; an area falling more than 2 points since the last run of the same kind fails R3.9, in part, D663 . - Coverage as graphs : a run's page shows a gauge against 90%, the areas least covered first, the trend over the last runs and the negative tests by kind; the same in the reports and a line in eax test R3.10, D664 . - Watch a test as it runs : Self-test ›"},{"t":"EA Explorer 2.0.0: Release 2","u":"releases/2.0.0.html","s":"","w":"Release 2 13 Nov 2026 : a menu bar that reaches every screen, testing that works in one command, sites and remote instances, the Docker engine, mounts and container files from the web with alerts when a container stops working , archived models and projects, backups proven by the self-test, and the fixes from the full self-tests. Before updating: take a backup .\\eax backup before-2.0.0 . From 1.0.0 the update runs migrations 0051 to 0067 new schemas such as operations, personal data, files, sites and the archive; indexes on every foreign key; nothing removed . After it, run .\\eax test full once: the Backups page enables its buttons when the backup checks pass. Known: three browser journeys can fail on a busy machine the tests' timing, not the screens ; they are R3.14. R2.0: a usable UI with a simple menu built 11 Nov 2026, to be accepted - A menu bar : Architecture Work, Model Admin, Project Admin, Repository & Content Framework the Architecture Repository and the Content framework together and System Admin, each a drop-down with sub-menus; on the right your own menu your name: your work, your profile, Sign out and ? help and documentation ; at the top left the site picker, ● Local Farm Admin . Last model and Last project side by side. Every screen, tab and wizard of 1.0 is in it a test checks nothing is left out . What you may not use is not shown D586, D588, D591 . - Wizards : click Wizards for the wizards page, or pick one wizard from its sub-menu D587, D591 . On a project page the Repository and Content framework tabs sit together. - Find: press / or Ctrl+K, or the box at the top for any function, with where it is in the menu, or content: models, projects and entities as you type, and Search everything D590 . - Menu Classic , a toggle at the top right: Classic keeps the menus of 1.0 for now. The left-menu tab style and the first sign-in question are gone D589 . This also answers R2.6 changing the layout did nothing on most pages . - Farm Admin Super Admins , from the site picker: Sites and Connect to a site, saying what R2.1 and R2.2 bring. See docs/r2-0-menu.md ../docs/r2-0-menu.md for where everything is. R2.0.1: testing that works, simply in progress - Two choices : the Smoke test or the Full test, on System Admin › Tools › Self-test or with eax test / eax test full . Each run starts its own test container, tests, reports and removes it D592 . - Test data cleaned up : each run removes what earlier runs left first; eax test clean and Delete all test data remove it at any time D593 . - Fixed : the self-test and updates stopping with \"the installation folder is not known\" the folder is now found from any of the installation's files the helper has, R2.8 ; the quality PDF and Excel of a model never measured; a malformed stakeholder id giving a server error; the change log's screen waiting behind its own set-up. - eax testbench is no longer a command CI keeps the test bench . - Model library and Project library for everyone : both in Architecture Work and Repository & Content Framework › Libraries ; the Project library has its own page, and library projects can be read by anyone with a role D594 . - Fixed : the Documentation page's documents and the library's EA Explorer documentation folder not found on an installation the documents were looked for in the document store's folder ; reports-init showing \"unhealthy\" after it finished R2.20 . A test run does not depend on the sample data or the industry packs D595 . - Fixed in the self-test D596 : the API writes run again they were all skipped ; the browser journeys wait for pop-ups, fields and choices on a slower computer; the test data is found on Windows. A server error now says what kind it was and its request id. The front door no longer lets other sites frame it or tells its nginx version. - Start-up finishes in one start D597 : the industry packs load file by file beside the sample data, with progress that moves; one file that fails no longer undoes the others; Reports no longer stays \"Created\". - Security D598 : newer cryptography, pypdf, draw.io 32.6.10 , Docker CLI and PostgreSQL images, and each image takes its distribution's fixes when built. - Fixed : making a gap analysis or a common analysis \"column domain does not exist\" ; a slow page or a project's download ending in a bare server error after 30 seconds. - Start-up D600 : the API no longer runs out of memory loading the industry packs one file at a time; 2 GB on a laptop ; Reports is up within minutes and loads its dashboards afterwards; a loader that stopped says so. - Containers : CPU is shown as a share of the whole machine, with the cores in use, so the total no longer passes 100% D601 . - Views : Standard views is the first sub-tab and opens by default; Custom views next. A model's picture opened in draw.io shows the objects on it and their properties, relationships and allowed relationships, read only D602, R2.7 . - Self-test results by importance D604 : every check critical or not, a ring chart and a functional health Healthy, Degraded, Not healthy in the report, on the Self-test page and at the end of eax test , with every failure listed. - The Reports tab \"Power BI and Excel\" is now OData ; the Classic button is gone D603 . - Run the failed ones again D605 : Self-test › History or a run's results, or eax test failed run --warnings : only the checks that failed, in fresh test data; the results show each check then and now, and the earlier run is marked followed up when all pass. The Command centre now also takes test full and test failed . - Fixed : on Windows, a self-test or command started from the web Self-test, Run the failed ones again, the Command centre could not start \"the working directory ... is invalid\" . A backup that cannot read a file now says which set and which file. - The Classic screens are gone D606 : the menu bar is the only menu; every page Classic reached is in it. - Fixed on Windows : Run the failed ones again, and anything the Self-test page"},{"t":"EA Explorer 1.0.0: Release 1","u":"releases/1.0.0.html","s":"","w":"The first release of EA Explorer: an open-source enterprise architecture repository AGPL-3.0 , installed and run on your own laptop, server or cloud. Release 1 is 0.19.0 with the last fixes; the full detail of each part is in 0.19.0 0.19.0.md and in the Documentation menu. What it does - A repository with a metamodel you control : ArchiMate 4 and TOGAF 10 built in, your own entity types, attributes including links , relationship rules with multiplicity and relationship attributes; models, child models, tags, history and compare. - Drawn views in draw.io , inside EA Explorer: two-way sync with the model, the ArchiMate notation, relationship tabs, name : type labels, undo; every picture of a model opens read only in our own draw.io save it as a drawn view or download it , and draw.io's Export as menu has a .drawio file D585 . - Keeping it clean : quality checks, duplicates found and merged, merging a child model into its parent, KPIs with trends, an OData feed and a report designer. - Projects on the TOGAF ADM : purpose, scope, phases and ADM iteration types, deliverables, key questions, governance log, sign-off, scenarios, surveys and EA capability maturity. - Industry reference models and packs : ten industries, with the books, workbooks and metamodel Excels to download. - Importing : published Excel and CSV formats, deliveries reviewed before loading, and a model from a metamodel workbook. - AI through MCP : about 120 tools for reading, analysing and changing models, each change previewed and confirmed, with an AI activity log. - Running it : eax deploy laptop, server, AWS, Azure, DigitalOcean , updates and rollback from the repository, backups and restore, machine access, operations insight, the Command centre and web console, schedules, a banner, settings that survive resets, on-screen help for every screen and the Documentation menu. Known limits, for Release 2 - The self-test System admin › Self-test, eax test and the outside test bench are on hold: they become one separate test container, the first thing in Release 2. - Start-up : on some installs the last sample-data steps and the industry-pack load into Documents do not finish; everything else works. Fixed in Release 2. - On-screen help does not show on the pages, changing the navigation layout does not change the screen, and a standard view opened in draw.io shows no stencil or object explorer. All three are fixed in Release 2. - In-place upgrade from System admin › Updates does not start the operations helper does not know the installation folder ; upgrade by pulling the new tag and running clean-restart until it is fixed in Release 2. - See docs/build-phases.md R2 for everything planned next. Before updating A fresh install: .\\eax clean-restart Windows or ./eax.sh clean-restart . From 0.19.0: update through System admin › Updates or eax update ; a full backup is taken first."},{"t":"EA Explorer 0.19.0","u":"releases/0.19.0.html","s":"","w":"The last set before version 1.0 D421 . What is new - Updates from the repository : System admin Updates and eax update move EA Explorer to a newer release, from the Prod, RC or Latest channel, with a full backup first, one release at a time, and Retry or Roll back if a step fails. - Releases : CI on every change, versioned releases with these notes, and a supported-versions policy. - Command centre System admin : every eax command from the browser, with a guided form, a Console for typing them and eax console 's menu and the history of every run; the same on eax deploy 's page. - Everything accepted up to 0.18.0: drawn views in draw.io, merge and dedupe, KPI trends, OData and the report designer, machine access, operations insight, surveys and maturity, import formats, industry models, MCP and scenario planning. Also in 0.19.0: banner, schedules, settings that survive resets - Banner System admin Banner : one message under the top bar, information, notice or urgent, with optional times and audience. Nothing shows unless an admin sets one. - Schedules System admin Command centre Schedules, eax schedule : eax commands that run by themselves, e.g. a nightly backup, a weekly smoke test, or Demo reset every night clean-restart laptop at 02:00 with a banner . - persist/ : schedules, the banner and safety backups live in a folder beside work/ that no reset deletes, as small JSON files you can read and edit; it is in every infrastructure backup. - Reset-survival test : eax test --reset-survival or the Self-test page's opt-in proves it with a real reset. Also in 0.19.0: relationship attributes and line labels - Relationships carry the attributes the metamodel defines, per relationship type or per allowed relationship D563, D564 , edited as key : value in the relationship list, a drawn view's line Properties, Excel and MCP; required ones are checked by quality. - Drawn view lines read name Type key:value … , and naming a line never hides its type; Line labels in the toolbar hides the values on busy diagrams D565 . - Migration 0047 adds the table that limits an attribute to some allowed relationships. Also in 0.19.0: ADM iteration types on projects - Each project's ADM cycle is a Full cycle or one of TOGAF's iterations: Architecture Capability Preliminary, A , Architecture Development B, C, D , Transition Planning E, F , Architecture Governance G, H , or Custom the phases you tick . Requirements Management is always open D571 . - The project page asks Which iteration is this? ; anyone on the project can change it at any time, with a history of every change D572 . - Phases left out are frozen : read only, never deleted, greyed on the ADM wheel and refused by the API D573 ; also in MCP, project backups, templates, the report, tasks and the self-test D574 . See docs/phase-iterations.md ../docs/phase-iterations.md . - Migration 0048 adds the table of iteration changes. Also in 0.19.0: a self-test that covers the whole app - Every page opens : the self-test opens every page, group, tab and sub-tab and checks each renders, has a heading and opens help on F1; the report says \"pages opened N of N\" D575 . - Real journeys click, type and save in the run's own fixtures, as each role allowed and refused to one that is not; the smoke test runs three of them D576 . - More checks : API writes area by area, and the same writes refused; database checks of history, values, relationship attribute mappings, drawn-view bindings and persist/ D577 . - A coverage summary opens every report. The Self-test page shows the exact eax test command for what you pick, with Copy, every command-line option, and the command each past run equals. New eax test --journey J and --pages-only D578 . - A bare Change documents page no longer says Loading... for ever found by the page sweep . - Migration 0049 keeps a run's journeys and pages-only choice. Also in 0.19.0: the test bench, testing from outside - eax testbench runs every self-test check from another machine against any EA Explorer address you own, as people reach it, with the same names and filters as eax test , in Chromium, Firefox, WebKit and Edge --browsers . It never runs without --target <address --i-own-this D579 . - It uses the self-test's own code and the target's own fixtures, and gives its results back to the Self-test history, marked external testbench ; --publish sends every result, also to another installation D580, D581 . - Install, upgrade and load : eax testbench install --answers … the deploy wizard , upgrade --from … --to … the version, the database migration and the data checked before and after and load --users … --minutes … k6, judged by testbench/thresholds.json D582 . - Reports in HTML, JSON and JUnit with a coverage summary; the exit code says whether it passed. - Test data for every test in testbench/data Excel and CSV deliveries, a metamodel workbook, documents, a survey, a drawn view, expected results , shared with the self-test /testdata in the test runner . - CI runs the API and UI suites on every change, and nightly an install, an upgrade from the previous release, every browser and a short load test. Every install guide ends with Check your installation docs/deployment.md ../docs/deployment.md check-your-installation ; see docs/testbench.md ../docs/testbench.md . Also in 0.19.0: starting and testing need no extra steps D584 - up and clean-restart prepare everything : the pack step copies new or changed industry packs from the pack source folders zips opened, duplicates once, quick when nothing changed , then the packs load into Documents with Industry packs loading n of N on the start-up page; set the sources once with eax packs source <folder or EAX PACKS SOURCE in the config. - Tests prepare their runner : every eax test and every Start on the Self-test page builds the test runner first seconds when current ; it is also built in the background at each start on by default . The page has no Build step any more Advanced keeps Rebuild . eax packs coll"},{"t":"Releases","u":"releases/index.html","s":"","w":"What came in each release, newest first. EA Explorer tells every installation about a new release on System Admin › Updates."}];
